ial intelligence on more-than-human relationships and political landscapes; highlight design-driven methods and investigations as political acts capable of regulating and fostering interdependent co-living, shaping materialities, and engaging with diverse epistemologies, ontologies, cosmologies, and relational practices. We encourage submissions across design, HCI, philosophy, and STS, aiming to cultivate a transdisciplinary dialogue. Download full call hereDownload Conference and panels: https://stsitalia.org/call-for-abstracts/#theme Submission: https://stsitalia.org/submission-2025/ First deadline: February 3rd, 2025 Important: There will not be a follow-up Call for Papers after this stage. Further dissemination: While no formal paper submissions will follow, alternative opportunities for sharing and publishing might be explored. Elisa Giaccardi, Valentina Rognoli, Emma Sicher, Francesco Nappo, Francesco Vergani, Laura Forlano, Martín Tironi (contact: elisa.giaccardi@polimi.it', 'Sources/Raw/designposthumanism/post-2851-panel-more-than-just-human-politics-of-relating-10th-sts-italia-conference.md', 'designposthumanism', 'https://designandposthumanism.org/archives/2851');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (64, 'Tactile Stories Project', 'https://designandposthumanism.org/archives/2878', 'designposthumanism', 'Sources/Raw/designposthumanism/post-2878-tactile-stories-project.md', '# Tactile Stories Project The image shows Kristine presenting the “Tactile Stories Toolkit” at the I.N.S.E.C.T. Summercamp 2024 @Svenja Keune The Tactile Stories Project invites you to tinker and play with vibro-haptic and tactile technologies and concepts. In a series of online workshops, we will develop and co-create interactive tactile sonic installations that we explore during the I.N.S.E.C.T. Summercamp 2025 and exhibit at the Earthbound Symposium, the MuseIT Final Event, and the 2025 CENSE Symposium. In addition to workshops, included in the program are online mingling with special guests in the fields of Social Haptic Communication and Biotremology (TBA). PROGRAM OVERVIEW Workshop 1 31st January 17:00 – 18:00 CET Introduction Workshop 2 27th February 17:00 – 18:00 CET Getting started Workshop 3 20th March 17:00 – 18:00 CET Tinker and Play Workshop 4 14th April 17:00 – 18:00 CET Present and Discuss Workshop 5 15th May 17:00 – 18:00 CET Project Work Project Discussions 2nd June 17:00 – 18:00 CET 7th July 17:00 – 18:00 CET I.N.S.E.C.T. Summercamp tba Hvalsø, Denmark Earthbound Symposium 19-21 August, Denmark MuseIT Final Event tba CENSE Symposium Beyond Listening, 23-26 September, Slovenia Reflection 3rd October 17:00 – 18:00 CET Looking back and Forward There is a sign-up fee of 70€ that supports the costs for the exhibitions. Please sign up via this form before January 24 to ensure your participation https://forms.gle/QjbMevvgW84HwBSJ8 and confirm your commitment to at least one of the exhibitions/interventions. The workshops will be recorded but you should be available for most of the dates to ensure a lively atmosphere and co-creation throughout this project. This project is facilitated by Kristine Diekman and Svenja Keune and an initiative by the VIBRA Research Network, which aims to explore the potentials of Biotremology, Inclusive Information Practices, and Research through Art and Design. Kristine Diekman is a media artist and educator. As an educator, she facilitates international workshops in digital storytelling and physical computing that lead participants through writing, craft, computing, and sound production to create interactive tactile audio interfaces to tell their stories. Dr. Svenja Keune is the VIBRA Research Network manager and facilitator of the I.N.S.E.C.T. Community and summer camp co-creations. She is a researcher always weaving new connections in between materials, practices, people, and fields of research.', '# Tactile Stories Project The image shows Kristine presenting the “Tactile Stories Toolkit” at the I.N.S.E.C.T. Summercamp 2024 @Svenja Keune The Tactile Stories Project invites you to tinker and play with vibro-haptic and tactile technologies and concepts. In a series of online workshops, we will develop and co-create interactive tactile sonic installations that we explore during the I.N.S.E.C.T. Summercamp 2025 and exhibit at the Earthbound Symposium, the MuseIT Final Event, and the 2025 CENSE Symposium. In addition to workshops, included in the program are online mingling with special guests in the fields of Social Haptic Communication and Biotremology (TBA). PROGRAM OVERVIEW Workshop 1 31st January 17:00 – 18:00 CET Introduction Workshop 2 27th February 17:00 – 18:00 CET Getting started Workshop 3 20th March 17:00 – 18:00 CET Tinker and Play Workshop 4 14th April 17:00 – 18:00 CET Pr');
