it lab open frameworks laser cutter big milling machine vacuum forming Materials cardboard 3mm hi density foam wood & veneer composites materials resins, bio -resins -plastics, epoxy etc fibers, cotton, hemp, linen, jute, etc vacuum bags Assignment Use software to obtain a body-figure and a digital fabrication process to produce it (the production happens in groups of 3-4) We recommend : For nodes that they need to have mannequins to exhibit their creations we suggest to create a more conventional figure that they can use. For nodes that already have mannequins, you can experiment with different figures and forms! How will it be evaluated? document use of a 3D scanner to acquire a model document repair of 3D model mesh experimented with the combination of milling, laser cutting, vacuum forming and composites built your own mannequin include all the files in the documentation Lecture notes Download the presentation Except where otherwise noted, content on this wiki is licensed under the following license: CC Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International', 'Sources/Raw/fabricademy/fabricademy2017classesdigitalbodies.md', 'fabricademy', 'http://wiki.textile-academy.org/fabricademy2017/classes/digitalbodies');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (131, 'fabricademy2017:classes:intro', 'http://wiki.textile-academy.org/fabricademy2017/classes/intro', 'fabricademy', 'Sources/Raw/fabricademy/fabricademy2017classesintro.md', '# fabricademy2017:classes:intro fabricademy2017 classes intro # Table of Contents 1. State of the art, Project Management and Documentation Lecture notes Documenting your work How to document Where to document Editing your student page How to upload an image # 1. State of the art, Project Management and Documentation September 26 2017 # Lecture notes What is Fabricademy State of the art Classes Why sharing How to document # Documenting your work # How to document Documentation is an important part of Fabricademy. You should document your work for your own, and for anybody who would like to replicate your work. You don''t need to repeat what has been explained during class, but document any issues and solutions you have found during your assignment. Make sure your documentation shows what you did as this is the primary reference for evaluating your work. # Where to document You can use this wiki as your documentation notebook. The wiki uses the DokuWiki software , check out the manual for more details. # Editing your student page Steps Find your student name in the students list Click on it to go to the student page If you didn''t create it before (the name will be in dashed underline) you will go to a <b>not found page.</b> Don''t worry! Click on the edit icon on the right and start editing your page. Fill in the information you need, like your profile and click Save . Repeat the process for editing your page Adding a new page can be done with the Link button. Select internal link and type in a name for your page. Save and then click on the link to create the new page. # How to upload an image Please make sure you upload only under the students folder , or you will get a permission error! Steps Edit the page where you want to include the image, clicking on the edit button on the right. Position the cursor where you want to put the image Click the image icon Browse server Click on the Choose file button, select the file on your computer and hit the upload button. Click on the image name to insert it Adjust the size of your image, changing the width Done Except where otherwise noted, content on this wiki is licensed under the following license: CC Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International', '# fabricademy2017:classes:intro fabricademy2017 classes intro # Table of Contents 1. State of the art, Project Management and Documentation Lecture notes Documenting your work How to document Where to document Editing your student page How to upload an image # 1. State of the art, Project Management and Documentation September 26 2017 # Lecture notes What is Fabricademy State of the art Classes Why sharing How to document # Documenting your work # How to document Documentation is an important part of Fabricademy. You should document your work for your own, and for anybody who would like to replicate your work. You don''t need to repeat what has been explained during class, but document any issues and solutions you have found during your assignment. Make sure your documentation shows what you did as this is the primary reference for evaluating your work. # Where to document You can use thi');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('fabricademy2017:classes:intro', '# fabricademy2017:classes:intro fabricademy2017 classes intro # Table of Contents 1. State of the art, Project Management and Documentation Lecture notes Documenting your work How to document Where to document Editing your student page How to upload an image # 1. State of the art, Project Management and Documentation September 26 2017 # Lecture notes What is Fabricademy State of the art Classes Why sharing How to document # Documenting your work # How to document Documentation is an important part of Fabricademy. You should document your work for your own, and for anybody who would like to replicate your work. You don''t need to repeat what has been explained during class, but document any issues and solutions you have found during your assignment. Make sure your documentation shows what you did as this is the primary reference for evaluating your work. # Where to document You can use this wiki as your documentation notebook. The wiki uses the DokuWiki software , check out the manual for more details. # Editing your student page Steps Find your student name in the students list Click on it to go to the student page If you didn''t create it before (the name will be in dashed underline) you will go to a <b>not found page.</b> Don''t worry! Click on the edit icon on the right and start editing your page. Fill in the information you need, like your profile and click Save . Repeat the process for editing your page Adding a new page can be done with the Link button. Select internal link and type in a name for your page. Save and then click on the link to create the new page. # How to upload an image Please make sure you upload only under the students folder , or you will get a permission error! Steps Edit the page where you want to include the image, clicking on the edit button on the right. Position the cursor where you want to put the image Click the image icon Browse server Click on the Choose file button, select the file on your computer and hit the upload button. Click on the image name to insert it Adjust the size of your image, changing the width Done Except where otherwise noted, content on this wiki is licensed under the following license: CC Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International', 'Sources/Raw/fabricademy/fabricademy2017classesintro.md', 'fabricademy', 'http://wiki.textile-academy.org/fabricademy2017/classes/intro');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (132, 'fabricademy2017:classes:opensourcehardware', 'http://wiki.textile-academy.org/fabricademy2017/classes/opensourcehardware', 'fabricademy', 'Sources/Raw/fabricademy/fabricademy2017classesopensourcehardware.md', '# fabricademy2017:classes:opensourcehardware fabricademy2017 classes opensourcehardware # Fabricademy 2017 # Open Source Hardware: From fibers to fabric Global Instructors: Mar Canet & Varvara Guljajeva The class explores the open source hardware field in general and focuses on its potential in the area of textile. How to update obsolete machines for producing textile? How to take advantage of digital fabrication and open source technology to come up with an open source machine for knitting, weaving and invent new techniques. This class focuses on the importance of the techniques, tools and machines that create traditional fabrics. The lecture will give an overview on the evolution of these tools and how these impact production and manufacturing, with the focus on hacking, both machines and tools, and creating open source accessible machinery for a broader public. Program outline Intro teachers Techniques & history Knitting History Knitting as first manufacturing home machine Weaving history Machines knitting machines mechanical electronic digital / industrial looms mechanical electronic digital industrial open source machines & hacking machines knitic circular knitic open knit → kniterate updating the industry with new tools, democratizing machines Tools Software: CAD / CAM Machines: laser cutter big milling machine electronics setup Lecture Notes Slides PDF Except where otherwise noted, content on this wiki is licensed under the following license: CC Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International', '# fabricademy2017:classes:opensourcehardware fabricademy2017 classes opensourcehardware # Fabricademy 2017 # Open Source Hardware: From fibers to fabric Global Instructors: Mar Canet & Varvara Guljajeva The class explores the open source hardware field in general and focuses on its potential in the area of textile. How to update obsolete machines for producing textile? How to take advantage of digital fabrication and open source technology to come up with an open source machine for knitting, weaving and invent new techniques. This class focuses on the importance of the techniques, tools and machines that create traditional fabrics. The lecture will give an overview on the evolution of these tools and how these impact production and manufacturing, with the focus on hacking, both machines and tools, and creating open source accessible machinery for a broader public. Program outline Intro t');
