 čišćenje za njima. Čuvajte i brinite o svoj imovini i opremi Radione. Opremu nemojte odnositi kući bez da niste prethodno pitali voditelje udruge. Dijeljenje i poklanjanje opreme udruge drugim ljudima bez znanja voditelja udruge ili Upravnog vijeća udruge nije dozvoljeno. Prijavite slomljene ili oštećene predmete voditeljima. Stvari se kvare zbog redovnog trošenja, samo ih želimo brzo popraviti ili zamijeniti! Nemojte donositi vlastitu opremu i projekte na dugotrajni boravak u prostor udruge ako niste sigurni da ćete imati vremena za bavljenje istim. Ako ipak donosite svoju opremu, držite je u kutiji jasno označenoj vašim imenom. Imajte na umu da su sve stvari koje donesete u Radionu tamo u potpunosti na vlastitu odgovornost. Nemojte koristiti opremu/vlasništvo drugih članova bez njihovog dopuštenja. Ako niste sigurni u vlasništvo nečega ili bi htjeli koristiti nešto što pripada nekom drugom, prvo pitajte tu osobu kojoj to pripada ili vodstvo udruge. Pri predlaganju projekata i promjena u prostoru uzmite u obzir dosadašnja iskustva Udruge ili se konzultirajte sa iskusnijim članovima Radione. Radiona funkcionira kao zajednica s višegodišnjim pozitivnim rezultatima. HVALA što se pridržavate ovih pravila! ENG Radiona – Zagreb Makerspace is an inclusive organisation and community where everyone is welcome and should feel safe. Everyone is expected to be friendly and respectful towards each other. This applies to all of Radiona’s physical meetings, events and the like, as well as all online communication channels and virtual activities. Non-members violating this code of conduct may be asked to leave immediately. Members violating this code of conduct may be subject to disciplinary proceedings including termination of membership. Everyone at Radiona, members or otherwise, are obliged to follow this code of conduct. Our lab is a safe and welcoming place for everyone, regardless of gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, disability, physical appearance, body size, age, race, nationality, ethnic minority, subculture, geographical region, knowledge, marital status, family status, social status or religion (or lack thereof), or technology choices. We expect everyone to maintain an environment of mutual respect, tolerance, encouragement and friendliness. Be nice to each other. Do not insult or act in a derogatory manner towards anyone else. Sexual language and imagery should only be used for positive purposes in accordance with best practices advocated by professional sex educators (if you’re not sure what those are, don’t do it). We do not tolerate harassment of people at our events or space in any form, including talks, workshops, performances, exhibitions, presentations and other online media (social media networks). Harassment includes offensive verbal comments related to gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, disability, physical appearance, body size, age, race, nationality, ethnic minority, subculture, geographical region, knowledge, technology choices, social status, religion, sexual images in public spaces (including slides and profile/avatar pictures), deliberate intimidation, stalking, following, harassing photography or recording, sustained disruption of talks or other events, inappropriate physical contact, and unwelcome sexual attention. You are expected to deal with disagreements in a friendly and respectful manner. People asked to stop any harassing behavior are expected to comply immediately. People violating these rules may be sanctioned or expelled from the space or the event at the discretion of any Radiona – Zagreb Makerspace member. If you wish to report harassment anonymously or privately, you can send a message to radiona.org (at) gmail.com Radiona has a clean as you go policy. You are expected to leave any work area, bench, desk, room etc. clean and tidy for the next person to use. Remember Radiona is a shared space. Leave the place as you would like to find it. Put tools, equipment and your property back in it’s place when you are finished. Report broken or damaged items to its owner or the directors. Stuff breaks through regular wear and tear, we just want to replace it quickly! If you bring visitors onto the premises, note that they may not clean up after themselves. As their host, you are responsible for cleaning up after them. Treat all property and equipment in the space with the same respect that you would treat your own property. Note however that your property at Radiona is there entirely at your own risk. Do not use other members property without their permission. If you are unsure as to ownership of something or whether to dispose of something, ask first. Visitors are not allowed to leave their property in the space. T H A N K Y O U for being nice!', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/page-1082-kodeks-ponašanja-code-of-conduct.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/about/code-of-conduct/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (210, 'About Radiona', 'https://radiona.org/about/about-radiona/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/page-1085-about-radiona.md', '# About Radiona Radiona.org je nezavisni art-tech laboratorij i community makerspace koji istražuje sjecišta umjetnosti, elektronike, otvorenog hardvera i suradničke kulture. Radiona.org is an independent art-tech lab and community makerspace exploring the intersections of art, electronics, open hardware, and collaborative culture. < >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< >< Otvoreni dana […] Radiona.org je nezavisni art-tech laboratorij i community makerspace koji istražuje sjecišta umjetnosti, elektronike, otvorenog hardvera i suradničke kulture. Radiona.org is an independent art-tech lab and community makerspace exploring the intersections of art, electronics, open hardware, and collaborative culture. < >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< >< Otvoreni dana laba: Ponedjeljkom i srijedom od 19:00 sati / OpenLab days: Mondays, 7pm; Wednesdays, 7pm. Za najavu rasporeda DailyLaba slijedi našu mrežnu stranicu ili društvene medije / Follow our website or social media for DailyLab schedule announcements. Lokacija laba / Lab Venue (mjesto gdje se odvijaju programi – radionice, meetupovi, predavanja, OpenLab i sl./a place where programs take place – workshops, meetups, lectures, OpenLab, etc.): Nova cesta 186 10000 Zagreb Hrvatska / Croatia Sjedište udruge / Official address of NGO (adresa gdje nam šaljete poštu/address where you are sending the post): Kozjačka 41 10090 Zagreb Hrvatska / Croatia Radionin mini lab teških industrija / Radiona Mini Lab of Heavy Industries (samo za članove udruge/only for lab members) Lastovska 2A 10000 Zagreb Hrvatska / Croatia IBAN: HR2123600001102369684 Bank sort code: 2360000 Swift: ZABAHR2X OIB13042216614 MB / ID: 4084586 Registarski broj / Register number: 21010465 >< >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< >< O Radioni Radiona.org – Udruga za razvoj “uradi-sam” kulture je nezavisni art-tech laboratorij, hackerspace i community makerspace sa sjedištem u Zagrebu. Osnovana 2011. godine, Radiona djeluje kao građanski laboratorij u kojem se umjetnost, tehnologija, znanost i društvo susreću kroz eksperimentalnu praksu, otvoreni hardver i suradničko učenje. Radiona okuplja umjetnike, inženjere, dizajnere, istraživače i entuzijaste zainteresirane za istraživanje tehnologije kroz praktičan rad i eksperiment. Organizacija razvija programe koji povezuju medijsku umjetnost, elektroniku, maker kulturu i društvene inovacije, potičući interdisciplinarnu razmjenu između kreativnih i tehničkih zajednica. Od osnutka do danas Radiona je organizirala više od 700 radionica, 50 izložbi, 8 međunarodnih kampova, 8 hackathona te cijeli niz predavanja i javnih događanja , surađujući s umjetnicima, istraživačima i organizacijama iz cijele Europe i šire. Kroz svoje programe i zajedničke inicijative Radiona je uključila tisuće sudionika te doprinijela razvoju aktivnog ekosustava makera, umjetnika, inženjera i učenika zainteresiranih za eksperimentalne tehnologije i otvoreno znanje. Radiona djeluje kao hibridna platforma koja uključuje makerspace i hackerspace, laboratorij za medijsku umjetnost, Repair Café inicijativu te program umjentičkih rezidencija. Kroz radionice, izložbe, istraživačke projekte, rezidencije i javna događanja Radiona potiče učenje kroz praksu te razvija kulturu DIY-a, DIWO-a (Do-It-With-Others) i DITO-a (Do-It-Together). Uz eksperimentalne programe umjetnosti i tehnologije, Radiona razvija inicijative inkluzivnog dizajna i asistivnih tehnologija kroz InkluLAB, program posvećen pristupačnosti, inkluzivnom obrazovanju i zajedničkom razvoju alata i tehnologija za osobe s invaliditetom. Radiona je posebno prepoznata po radu u području kreativne elektronike, kulture sintisajzera, otvorenog hardvera, eksperimentalnih instrumenata, digitalne fabrikacije i hibridnih umjetničkih praksi koje povezuju umjetničko istraživanje s tehnološkim eksperimentom. Edukacija i razmjena znanja nalaze se u središtu Radionine misije. Kroz radionice, rezidencije, community programe, aktivnosti InkluLAB-a i Repair Café inicijativu organizacija promiče neformalno i međugeneracijsko učenje kroz STEAM pristup, pristupačne tehnologije i inicijative koje dolaze iz zajednice. Spajajući umjetnost, tehnologiju, otvoreno znanje i suradničku kulturu, Radiona djeluje kao platforma za eksperiment, razmjenu znanja i izgradnju zajednice unutar šireg europskog ekosustava nezavisnih art-tech laboratorija . – Radiona : https://radiona.org/ – Laboratorij društvene uključenosti i kohezije – InkluLAB: https://inklulab.eu/ – Međunarodni maker kamp : Electric Wonderland – https://www.electric-wonderland.eu/ – Internet portal za zelene kulture: https://greenoteka.eu/ – Hacktonauts: https://hacktonauts.net/ >< >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< >< ENGLISH About Radiona Radiona.org – Association for Development of “Do-It-Yourself” Culture is an independent art-tech lab, hackerspace and community makerspace based in Zagreb, Croatia. Founded in 2011, Radiona operates as a citizen laboratory where art, technology, science and society intersect through experimental practice, open hardware and collaborative learning. Radiona brings together artists, engineers, designers, researchers and enthusiasts interested in exploring technologies through hands-on experimentation. The organisation develops programs that connect media art, electronics, maker culture and social innovation, fostering interdisciplinary exchange between creative and technical communities. Since its founding, Radiona has organised more than 700 workshops, 50 exhibitions, 8 international camps, 8 hackathons , as well as numerous lectures and public events, collaborating with artists, researchers and organisations across Europe and beyond. Through its programs and collaborative initiatives, Radiona has engaged thousands of participants and contributed to the development of an active ecosystem of makers, artists, engineers and learners interested in experimental technologies and open knowledge. Radiona operates as a hybrid platform that includes a makerspace and hackerspace, a media art laboratory, a Repair Café initiative and an artist-in-residence program . Through workshops, exhibitions, research projects, residencies and public events, Radiona encourages learning by doing and supports DIY, DIWO (Do-It-With-Others) and DITO (Do-It-Together) cultures. In addition to its experimental art and technology programs, Radiona develops inclusive design and assistive technology initiatives through InkluLAB , a program dedicated to accessibility, inclusive education and the collaborative development of tools and technologies for people with disabilities. Radiona is particularly recognised for its work in creative electronics, synthesizer culture, open hardware, experimental instruments, digital fabrication and hybrid art practices that connect artistic exploration with technological experimentation. Education and knowledge-sharing are central to Radiona’s mission. Through workshops, residencies, community programs, InkluLAB activities and its Repair Café initiative, the organisation promotes informal and intergenerational learning through STEAM approaches, accessible technologies and community-driven initiatives. By combining art, technology, open knowledge and collaborative culture, Radiona acts as a platform for experimentation, knowledge exchange and community building within the broader European ecosystem of independent art-tech laboratories . – Radiona: https://radiona.org/ – Social inclusion and cohesion lab – InkluLAB – https://inklulab.eu/ – International maker camp: Electric Wonderland – https://www.electric- wonderland.eu/ – Web portal for green cultures: https://greenoteka.eu/ – Hacktonauts: https://hacktonauts.net/', '# About Radiona Radiona.org je nezavisni art-tech laboratorij i community makerspace koji istražuje sjecišta umjetnosti, elektronike, otvorenog hardvera i suradničke kulture. Radiona.org is an independent art-tech lab and community makerspace exploring the intersections of art, electronics, open hardware, and collaborative culture. < >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< >< Otvoreni dana […] Radiona.org je nezavisni art-tech laboratorij i community makerspace koji istražuje sjecišta umjetnosti, elektronike, otvorenog hardvera i suradničke kulture. Radiona.org is an independent art-tech lab and community makerspace exploring the intersections of art, electronics, open hardware, and collaborative culture. < >< >< >< >< >< >< ><>< >< >< >< >< >< >< >< Otvoreni dana laba: Ponedjeljkom i srijedom od 19:00 sati / OpenLab days: Mondays, 7pm; Wednesdays, 7pm. Za najavu rasporeda DailyLaba sli');
