n: – općom uplatnicom ili e-bankarstvom – pod platitelj upišite svoje podatke (ime, prezime i adresu) – pod primatelj upišite Udruga za razvoj ‘uradi sam’ kulture – Radiona, Kozjačka 41, 10 090 Zagreb, na račun: IBAN: HR2123600001102369684 – opis plaćanja: uvijek navedite naziv radionice (Radionica Rat Synth) – kopiju uplatnice donosite prvi dan radionice i predajete voditelju radionice ili šaljete na e-mail: edu.radiona.org@gmail.com – GOTOVINU NE PRIMAMO O voditelju: Alwin Weber aka “StöRenfrieD” njemački je umjetnik iz Dresdena. Eksperimentira sa zvukom od 2001. godine, a tehnikom circuit bending počinje se baviti u 2007. godini. Rezultati njegovih hakerskih procesa dovode do osnivanja projekta i serije koncerata i radionica pod nazivom CircuitCircle (2009.). Od tada nastupa i izlaže svoje instalacije na brojnim festivalima u Europi, poput Cynet Art Festival, Ars Electronica i dr. Web: http://circuitcircle.de/ Podržali: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske Grad Zagreb Zaklada Kultura nova //////////////////////////////////////////////// Squeaking Rat Synth – workshop We are building the Squeaking Rat synthesizer at a workshop led by German artist Alwin Weber, which will take place on Thursday, May 29, 2025, from 6 pm at Radiona.org. In the workshop we are building the „Squaking Rat“. Its a standalone synth, based on the good old Cmos 4093 NAND Gate chip. There are 4 oscillators, where two work more as modulators and two are the main frequency. The sound range goes from subby bass till annoying squeaky stuff. Furthermore we talking about Circuits and Graphics and how a PCB is designed and produced from DIY level to a large production scale. Where to start and how to finish a circuit project. You also have the possibility to “solder a solderiron”. “SillySolderSynth”, it´s a based on an attiny microcontroler and creating weird sounds and bleeps. Its shaped like an solderiron and its the ultimate nerd gadget. Make it a bling bling device and put it on a chain or wear it as a stylish sound device on your belt! You can register until Thursday, May 29, 2025 at midnight at the link: https://forms.gle/WwSLGYayhfacDKM37 The registration fee is 20 EURO and you take your synth home. After confirming your place at the workshop, you can pay for it in the following way: – by general payment slip or e-banking – under the payer, enter your details (name, surname and address) – under the recipient, enter the Association for the Development of DIY Culture – Radiona, Kozjačka 41, 10 090 Zagreb, to the account: IBAN: HR2123600001102369684 – payment description: always state the name of the workshop (Squeaking Rat Synth) – bring a copy of the payment slip on the first day of the workshop and hand it over to the workshop leader or send it to: edu.radiona.org@gmail.com – WE DO NOT ACCEPT CASH Alwin Weber aka “StöRenfrieD” is a German artist from Dresden. He has been experimenting with sound since 2001, and started working with the circuit bending technique in 2007. The results of his hacking processes lead to the founding of a project and series of concerts and workshops called CircuitCircle (2009). Since then, he has performed and exhibited his installations at numerous festivals in Europe, such as Cynet Art Festival, Ars Electronica, etc. He is also orginiser of several DIY/DIWO electronic music festivals in Dresden. Web: http://circuitcircle.de/ Support: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia City of Zagreb Kultura Nova Foundation', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10703-škripajući-štakor-sint-squeaking-rat-synth-radionica-workshop.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/skripajuci-stakor-sint-squeaking-rat-synth-radionica-workshop/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (243, 'Radionica/Workshop: Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri', 'https://radiona.org/radionica-workshop-circuit-bending-pcb-potpourri/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10710-radionica-workshop-circuit-bending-pcb-potpourri.md', '# Radionica/Workshop: Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Radionica Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri Alwina Webera održat će se u petak, 30. svibnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Na radionici imate mogućnost modificirati igračku, zvučni uređaj ili druge postojeće sklopove kako biste postali neobičan “Izvanzemaljski instrument”. Tehnika se naziva circuit bending i zabavan je način za početak […] RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Radionica Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri Alwina Webera održat će se u petak, 30. svibnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Na radionici imate mogućnost modificirati igračku, zvučni uređaj ili druge postojeće sklopove kako biste postali neobičan “Izvanzemaljski instrument”. Tehnika se naziva circuit bending i zabavan je način za početak bavljenja elektronikom i izgradnju vlastitog eksperimentalnog elektroničkog instrumenta. Potpuno je praktična, a kao metoda pokušaja i pogrešaka vrlo je razigran način ulaska u temu elektronike. Možete donijeti vlastite igračke i zvučne uređaje, ali bit će osigurane i stvari. Što stariji to bolji. Druga polovica radionice je “PCB Potpourri”. Radi se o savijanju sklopova starih sklopova Alwina Webera i spajanju različitih ploča i funkcija već postojećih uređaja. Alwin donosi neke starije tiskane ploče, probne ploče i mnoštvo komponenti. Cilj je stvoriti vlastitu malu postavku buke ili zvučnu skulpturu i dobiti uvid u određene funkcije sklopova iz CircuitCirclea i osnovne zvučne sklopove općenito. RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Prijaviti se možete četvrtka, 29. svibnja 2025. točno u ponoć na poveznici: https://forms.gle/GFcDFwNAR6b8GVJQ8 Kotizacija: 15 EUR O voditelju: Alwin Weber aka “StöRenfrieD” njemački je umjetnik iz Dresdena. Eksperimentira sa zvukom od 2001. godine, a tehnikom circuit bending počinje se baviti u 2007. godini. Rezultati njegovih hakerskih procesa dovode do osnivanja projekta i serije koncerata i radionica pod nazivom CircuitCircle (2009.). Od tada nastupa i izlaže svoje instalacije na brojnim festivalima u Europi, poput Cynet Art Festival, Ars Electronica i dr. Web: http://circuitcircle.de/ Podržali: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske Grad Zagreb Zaklada Kultura nova ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////// “Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri” Workshop Alwin Weber’s Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri workshop will be held on Friday, May 30, 2025 from 6pm in the Workshop. In the workshop you have the possibility to modify a toy, a sound device or other existing circuits to become a weird “Alien Instrument”. The technique is called circuit bending and its a fun way to start with electronics and building your first own experimental electronic instrument. It´s totally hands on and the trial and error method is a very playful way to get into the topic. You can bring your own toys and sound devices but there will also be stuff provided. The older the better. The other half of the workshop is the “PCB Potpourri”. Its about circuit bending old circuits of Alwin Weber and mash up different boards and functions of already existing devices. Alwin is bringing some older circuit boards, breadboards and loads of components. The goal is to create your own little noise setup or soundsculpture and get an inview about certain functions of the circuits from CircuitCircle and basic sound circuits in general. You can register on Thursday, May 29, 2025 at midnight at the following link: https://forms.gle/GFcDFwNAR6b8GVJQ8 Registration fee: 15 EUR Alwin Weber aka “StöRenfrieD” is a German artist from Dresden. He has been experimenting with sound since 2001, and started working with the circuit bending technique in 2007. The results of his hacking processes lead to the founding of a project and series of concerts and workshops called CircuitCircle (2009). Since then, he has performed and exhibited his installations at numerous festivals in Europe, such as Cynet Art Festival, Ars Electronica, etc. He is also orginiser of several DIY/DIWO electronic music festivals in Dresden. Web: http://circuitcircle.de/ Support: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia City of Zagreb Kultura Nova Foundation', '# Radionica/Workshop: Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Radionica Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri Alwina Webera održat će se u petak, 30. svibnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Na radionici imate mogućnost modificirati igračku, zvučni uređaj ili druge postojeće sklopove kako biste postali neobičan “Izvanzemaljski instrument”. Tehnika se naziva circuit bending i zabavan je način za početak […] RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Radionica Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri Alwina Webera održat će se u petak, 30. svibnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Na radionici imate mogućnost modificirati igračku, zvučni uređaj ili druge postojeće sklopove kako biste postali neobičan “Izvanzemaljski instrument”. Tehnika se naziva circuit bending i zabavan je način za početak bavljenja elektronikom i izgradnju vlastitog eksperimentalnog elektroničkog instrumenta.');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Radionica/Workshop: Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri', '# Radionica/Workshop: Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Radionica Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri Alwina Webera održat će se u petak, 30. svibnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Na radionici imate mogućnost modificirati igračku, zvučni uređaj ili druge postojeće sklopove kako biste postali neobičan “Izvanzemaljski instrument”. Tehnika se naziva circuit bending i zabavan je način za početak […] RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Radionica Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri Alwina Webera održat će se u petak, 30. svibnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Na radionici imate mogućnost modificirati igračku, zvučni uređaj ili druge postojeće sklopove kako biste postali neobičan “Izvanzemaljski instrument”. Tehnika se naziva circuit bending i zabavan je način za početak bavljenja elektronikom i izgradnju vlastitog eksperimentalnog elektroničkog instrumenta. Potpuno je praktična, a kao metoda pokušaja i pogrešaka vrlo je razigran način ulaska u temu elektronike. Možete donijeti vlastite igračke i zvučne uređaje, ali bit će osigurane i stvari. Što stariji to bolji. Druga polovica radionice je “PCB Potpourri”. Radi se o savijanju sklopova starih sklopova Alwina Webera i spajanju različitih ploča i funkcija već postojećih uređaja. Alwin donosi neke starije tiskane ploče, probne ploče i mnoštvo komponenti. Cilj je stvoriti vlastitu malu postavku buke ili zvučnu skulpturu i dobiti uvid u određene funkcije sklopova iz CircuitCirclea i osnovne zvučne sklopove općenito. RADIONICA JE POPUNJENA! HVALA NA RAZUMIJEVANJU! Prijaviti se možete četvrtka, 29. svibnja 2025. točno u ponoć na poveznici: https://forms.gle/GFcDFwNAR6b8GVJQ8 Kotizacija: 15 EUR O voditelju: Alwin Weber aka “StöRenfrieD” njemački je umjetnik iz Dresdena. Eksperimentira sa zvukom od 2001. godine, a tehnikom circuit bending počinje se baviti u 2007. godini. Rezultati njegovih hakerskih procesa dovode do osnivanja projekta i serije koncerata i radionica pod nazivom CircuitCircle (2009.). Od tada nastupa i izlaže svoje instalacije na brojnim festivalima u Europi, poput Cynet Art Festival, Ars Electronica i dr. Web: http://circuitcircle.de/ Podržali: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske Grad Zagreb Zaklada Kultura nova ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////// “Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri” Workshop Alwin Weber’s Circuit Bending + PCB Potpourri workshop will be held on Friday, May 30, 2025 from 6pm in the Workshop. In the workshop you have the possibility to modify a toy, a sound device or other existing circuits to become a weird “Alien Instrument”. The technique is called circuit bending and its a fun way to start with electronics and building your first own experimental electronic instrument. It´s totally hands on and the trial and error method is a very playful way to get into the topic. You can bring your own toys and sound devices but there will also be stuff provided. The older the better. The other half of the workshop is the “PCB Potpourri”. Its about circuit bending old circuits of Alwin Weber and mash up different boards and functions of already existing devices. Alwin is bringing some older circuit boards, breadboards and loads of components. The goal is to create your own little noise setup or soundsculpture and get an inview about certain functions of the circuits from CircuitCircle and basic sound circuits in general. You can register on Thursday, May 29, 2025 at midnight at the following link: https://forms.gle/GFcDFwNAR6b8GVJQ8 Registration fee: 15 EUR Alwin Weber aka “StöRenfrieD” is a German artist from Dresden. He has been experimenting with sound since 2001, and started working with the circuit bending technique in 2007. The results of his hacking processes lead to the founding of a project and series of concerts and workshops called CircuitCircle (2009). Since then, he has performed and exhibited his installations at numerous festivals in Europe, such as Cynet Art Festival, Ars Electronica, etc. He is also orginiser of several DIY/DIWO electronic music festivals in Dresden. Web: http://circuitcircle.de/ Support: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia City of Zagreb Kultura Nova Foundation', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10710-radionica-workshop-circuit-bending-pcb-potpourri.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/radionica-workshop-circuit-bending-pcb-potpourri/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (244, 'Artist-in-Residence: Constanza Piña – THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR', 'https://radiona.org/artist-in-residence-constanza-pina-the-heart-is-an-oscillator/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10717-artist-in-residence-constanza-piña-the-heart-is-an-oscillator.md', '# Artist-in-Residence: Constanza Piña – THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR Chilean artist based in Berlin, Constanza Piña is partaking artist-in-residence program in Radiona during May/June 2025. Her residence title is THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR | DIY love synths and electronic anarchy. The Heart is an Oscillator” is a Corazón de Robota residency at Radiona focused on collecting and documenting recent electronic experiments. The goal is to open the heart […] Chilean artist based in Berlin, Constanza Piña is partaking artist-in-residence program in Radiona during May/June 2025. Her residence title is THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR | DIY love synths and electronic anarchy. The Heart is an Oscillator” is a Corazón de Robota residency at Radiona focused on collecting and documenting recent electronic experiments. The goal is to open the heart source of the electronics and make resources available to the noise community. The residency aims to develop a series of educational DIY synthesizer kits that will include s chematics and PCB designs, l ists of accessible material kits, s tep-by-step and assembly tutorials to create comprehensive guides that empower anyone to build their own instruments for noise generation. Additionally, Corazón de Robota will offer a public workshop showcasing a new device created during the residency. In this workshop, the entire development process will be shared, from conceptualisation to final build, providing a practical and educational experience for all attendees. Constanza Piña aka Corazón de Robota is a sound electronic artist and independent educator originally from Curicó, Chile. Her work is based on electronic experimentation, open source technologies, DIY philosophy and techno feminist social practices. She explores noise as a sonic, political, cultural and spiritual phenomenon. Interested in recycling, hardware hacking, soft-circuits, DIY antennas, handicrafts synths, ancestral technologies, and electronic wizardry, Constanza is active in the underground music scene since 2010 under the pseudonym Corazón de Robota (She-Robot Heart)she exclusively uses her self-built DIY synthesizers to explore the field of audible and inaudible frequencies, the psycho-physical perceptions of sound, and the rhythmic dimensions of noise. One of her standout projects, “Khipu | Pre-Electrotextile Hispanic Computer,” was awarded at the Ars Electronica Prix 2020 and reimagines Andean knowledge systems through a science fiction lens. It’s all about reclaiming and validating knowledge that’s often sidelined by mainstream science. Constanza ’s work has been exhibited around the world—from MOLAA in Los Angeles to ZKM in Germany, Sonar+D in Spain, FILE in Brazil, and at museums and cultural spaces across Latin America, Europe, Asia, and North America. She also founded Cyborgrrrls (@cyborgrrrls), a technofeminist meeting focused on building feminist and subversive tech spaces. Today, she works independently as an artist and educator through her project Non Binary Electronic Berlin. Support: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia City of Zagreb Kultura Nova Foundation', '# Artist-in-Residence: Constanza Piña – THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR Chilean artist based in Berlin, Constanza Piña is partaking artist-in-residence program in Radiona during May/June 2025. Her residence title is THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR | DIY love synths and electronic anarchy. The Heart is an Oscillator” is a Corazón de Robota residency at Radiona focused on collecting and documenting recent electronic experiments. The goal is to open the heart […] Chilean artist based in Berlin, Constanza Piña is partaking artist-in-residence program in Radiona during May/June 2025. Her residence title is THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR | DIY love synths and electronic anarchy. The Heart is an Oscillator” is a Corazón de Robota residency at Radiona focused on collecting and documenting recent electronic experiments. The goal is to open the heart source of the electronics and make resources available to the');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Artist-in-Residence: Constanza Piña – THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR', '# Artist-in-Residence: Constanza Piña – THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR Chilean artist based in Berlin, Constanza Piña is partaking artist-in-residence program in Radiona during May/June 2025. Her residence title is THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR | DIY love synths and electronic anarchy. The Heart is an Oscillator” is a Corazón de Robota residency at Radiona focused on collecting and documenting recent electronic experiments. The goal is to open the heart […] Chilean artist based in Berlin, Constanza Piña is partaking artist-in-residence program in Radiona during May/June 2025. Her residence title is THE HEART IS AN OSCILLATOR | DIY love synths and electronic anarchy. The Heart is an Oscillator” is a Corazón de Robota residency at Radiona focused on collecting and documenting recent electronic experiments. The goal is to open the heart source of the electronics and make resources available to the noise community. The residency aims to develop a series of educational DIY synthesizer kits that will include s chematics and PCB designs, l ists of accessible material kits, s tep-by-step and assembly tutorials to create comprehensive guides that empower anyone to build their own instruments for noise generation. Additionally, Corazón de Robota will offer a public workshop showcasing a new device created during the residency. In this workshop, the entire development process will be shared, from conceptualisation to final build, providing a practical and educational experience for all attendees. Constanza Piña aka Corazón de Robota is a sound electronic artist and independent educator originally from Curicó, Chile. Her work is based on electronic experimentation, open source technologies, DIY philosophy and techno feminist social practices. She explores noise as a sonic, political, cultural and spiritual phenomenon. Interested in recycling, hardware hacking, soft-circuits, DIY antennas, handicrafts synths, ancestral technologies, and electronic wizardry, Constanza is active in the underground music scene since 2010 under the pseudonym Corazón de Robota (She-Robot Heart)she exclusively uses her self-built DIY synthesizers to explore the field of audible and inaudible frequencies, the psycho-physical perceptions of sound, and the rhythmic dimensions of noise. One of her standout projects, “Khipu | Pre-Electrotextile Hispanic Computer,” was awarded at the Ars Electronica Prix 2020 and reimagines Andean knowledge systems through a science fiction lens. It’s all about reclaiming and validating knowledge that’s often sidelined by mainstream science. Constanza ’s work has been exhibited around the world—from MOLAA in Los Angeles to ZKM in Germany, Sonar+D in Spain, FILE in Brazil, and at museums and cultural spaces across Latin America, Europe, Asia, and North America. She also founded Cyborgrrrls (@cyborgrrrls), a technofeminist meeting focused on building feminist and subversive tech spaces. Today, she works independently as an artist and educator through her project Non Binary Electronic Berlin. Support: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia City of Zagreb Kultura Nova Foundation', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10717-artist-in-residence-constanza-piña-the-heart-is-an-oscillator.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/artist-in-residence-constanza-pina-the-heart-is-an-oscillator/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (245, 'Ruksak pun kulture 2025. – Radiona Theremin Postcard', 'https://radiona.org/ruksak-pun-kulture-2025-radiona-theremin-postcard/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10724-ruksak-pun-kulture-2025-radiona-theremin-postcard.md', '# Ruksak pun kulture 2025. – Radiona Theremin Postcard Radiona.org sudjeluje u programu Ruksak pun kulture za 2025. Ministarstva kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske održavajući radionice tijekom godine u Osnovna škola Mahično i Centru za odgoj i obrazovanje djece i mladeži u Karlovcu. U sklopu programa realiziramo radionice Radiona Theremin Postcard koje smo namijenili za tu priliku za tinejdžere – osmi razredi osnovne škole […] Radiona.org sudjeluje u programu Ruksak pun kulture za 2025. Ministarstva kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske održavajući radionice tijekom godine u Osnovna škola Mahično i Centru za odgoj i obrazovanje djece i mladeži u Karlovcu. U sklopu programa realiziramo radionice Radiona Theremin Postcard koje smo namijenili za tu priliku za tinejdžere – osmi razredi osnovne škole i prvi raazredi srednjih škola. Program se također provodio u sklopu poziva od 2020.-2024. godine. Voditeljica radionica je Deborah Hustić. Radiona Theremin Postcard radionica do sad je predstavljena u domaćem i međunarodnom okruženju. Prve radionice održale su se u sklopu stručnog kongresa Kulturna edukacija – Umjetnost u tehnologiji u travnju 2019. godine u Amsterdamu za koju je program bio i osmišljen. Kongres je bio namijenjen nastavnicima likovne kulture i umjetnosti, a odvio se u organizaciji Mocca Amsterdam – mreže eksperata za kulturnu edukaciju. Više o tome ovdje: https://radiona.org/radiona-mocca-amsterdam-conference/ Dizajn potpisuje Damir Prizmić prema prijedlogu voditeljice radionice.', '# Ruksak pun kulture 2025. – Radiona Theremin Postcard Radiona.org sudjeluje u programu Ruksak pun kulture za 2025. Ministarstva kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske održavajući radionice tijekom godine u Osnovna škola Mahično i Centru za odgoj i obrazovanje djece i mladeži u Karlovcu. U sklopu programa realiziramo radionice Radiona Theremin Postcard koje smo namijenili za tu priliku za tinejdžere – osmi razredi osnovne škole […] Radiona.org sudjeluje u programu Ruksak pun kulture za 2025. Ministarstva kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske održavajući radionice tijekom godine u Osnovna škola Mahično i Centru za odgoj i obrazovanje djece i mladeži u Karlovcu. U sklopu programa realiziramo radionice Radiona Theremin Postcard koje smo namijenili za tu priliku za tinejdžere – osmi razredi osnovne škole i prvi raazredi srednjih škola. Program se također provodio u sklopu poziva od 2020.-2024. go');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Ruksak pun kulture 2025. – Radiona Theremin Postcard', '# Ruksak pun kulture 2025. – Radiona Theremin Postcard Radiona.org sudjeluje u programu Ruksak pun kulture za 2025. Ministarstva kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske održavajući radionice tijekom godine u Osnovna škola Mahično i Centru za odgoj i obrazovanje djece i mladeži u Karlovcu. U sklopu programa realiziramo radionice Radiona Theremin Postcard koje smo namijenili za tu priliku za tinejdžere – osmi razredi osnovne škole […] Radiona.org sudjeluje u programu Ruksak pun kulture za 2025. Ministarstva kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske održavajući radionice tijekom godine u Osnovna škola Mahično i Centru za odgoj i obrazovanje djece i mladeži u Karlovcu. U sklopu programa realiziramo radionice Radiona Theremin Postcard koje smo namijenili za tu priliku za tinejdžere – osmi razredi osnovne škole i prvi raazredi srednjih škola. Program se također provodio u sklopu poziva od 2020.-2024. godine. Voditeljica radionica je Deborah Hustić. Radiona Theremin Postcard radionica do sad je predstavljena u domaćem i međunarodnom okruženju. Prve radionice održale su se u sklopu stručnog kongresa Kulturna edukacija – Umjetnost u tehnologiji u travnju 2019. godine u Amsterdamu za koju je program bio i osmišljen. Kongres je bio namijenjen nastavnicima likovne kulture i umjetnosti, a odvio se u organizaciji Mocca Amsterdam – mreže eksperata za kulturnu edukaciju. Više o tome ovdje: https://radiona.org/radiona-mocca-amsterdam-conference/ Dizajn potpisuje Damir Prizmić prema prijedlogu voditeljice radionice.', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10724-ruksak-pun-kulture-2025-radiona-theremin-postcard.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/ruksak-pun-kulture-2025-radiona-theremin-postcard/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (246, 'Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025 selections made', 'https://radiona.org/rewilding-cultures-mobility-conversation-2025-selections-made/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10729-rewilding-cultures-mobility-conversation-2025-selections-made.md', '# Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025 selections made We want to thank everyone who applied for the Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025. The selection panel, made up of representatives from Rewilding Cultures partner organisations, have now reviewed all of the applications and collectively made a decision on who to award the eight available grants to. From the over 80 application received via the […] We want to thank everyone who applied for the Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025. The selection panel, made up of representatives from Rewilding Cultures partner organisations, have now reviewed all of the applications and collectively made a decision on who to award the eight available grants to. From the over 80 application received via the open call, Anni Puolakka (Cultivamos Cultura), Catherine Lenoble (Makery), Kim Doan Quoc (Ionian University), Ren Loren Britton (Schmiede Hallein), Thomas Preindl (Projekt Atol), Dharmendra Prasad (Bioart Society), Liora Moser (Culture Yard), and Gemma Ciabattoni (Radiona) were selected. Rewilding Cultures (RC) is a Creative Europe collaboration project, which wants to reposition the wild within the field of art practices connecting to science and technology. As the European cultural sector has been and still is affected by multiple subsequent and coincident crises (incl. COVID-19, war-induced inflation, migration) we need to rewild on terms fit for the present and future. Rewilding Cultures is co-funded by the Creative Europe programme of the European Union, which aims to support European projects in the field of cultural production and innovation. The partner associations include ART2M / Makery (FR), Bioart Society (FI), The Culture Yard (DK), Cultivamos Cultura (PT), Ionian University (GR), Radiona (HR), Schmiede Hallein (AT) and Projekt Atol (SI) which leads the project. More information on the project available on the Rewilding Cultures website . (Source: Bioart Society)', '# Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025 selections made We want to thank everyone who applied for the Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025. The selection panel, made up of representatives from Rewilding Cultures partner organisations, have now reviewed all of the applications and collectively made a decision on who to award the eight available grants to. From the over 80 application received via the […] We want to thank everyone who applied for the Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025. The selection panel, made up of representatives from Rewilding Cultures partner organisations, have now reviewed all of the applications and collectively made a decision on who to award the eight available grants to. From the over 80 application received via the open call, Anni Puolakka (Cultivamos Cultura), Catherine Lenoble (Makery), Kim Doan Quoc (Ionian University), Ren Loren ');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025 selections made', '# Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025 selections made We want to thank everyone who applied for the Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025. The selection panel, made up of representatives from Rewilding Cultures partner organisations, have now reviewed all of the applications and collectively made a decision on who to award the eight available grants to. From the over 80 application received via the […] We want to thank everyone who applied for the Rewilding Cultures Mobility Conversation 2025. The selection panel, made up of representatives from Rewilding Cultures partner organisations, have now reviewed all of the applications and collectively made a decision on who to award the eight available grants to. From the over 80 application received via the open call, Anni Puolakka (Cultivamos Cultura), Catherine Lenoble (Makery), Kim Doan Quoc (Ionian University), Ren Loren Britton (Schmiede Hallein), Thomas Preindl (Projekt Atol), Dharmendra Prasad (Bioart Society), Liora Moser (Culture Yard), and Gemma Ciabattoni (Radiona) were selected. Rewilding Cultures (RC) is a Creative Europe collaboration project, which wants to reposition the wild within the field of art practices connecting to science and technology. As the European cultural sector has been and still is affected by multiple subsequent and coincident crises (incl. COVID-19, war-induced inflation, migration) we need to rewild on terms fit for the present and future. Rewilding Cultures is co-funded by the Creative Europe programme of the European Union, which aims to support European projects in the field of cultural production and innovation. The partner associations include ART2M / Makery (FR), Bioart Society (FI), The Culture Yard (DK), Cultivamos Cultura (PT), Ionian University (GR), Radiona (HR), Schmiede Hallein (AT) and Projekt Atol (SI) which leads the project. More information on the project available on the Rewilding Cultures website . (Source: Bioart Society)', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10729-rewilding-cultures-mobility-conversation-2025-selections-made.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/rewilding-cultures-mobility-conversation-2025-selections-made/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (247, 'Corazón de Robota: Radionica – Srčani sint / Heart Synth Workshop', 'https://radiona.org/corazon-de-robota-radionica-srcani-sint-heart-synth-workshop/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10737-corazón-de-robota-radionica-srčani-sint-heart-synth-workshop.md', '# Corazón de Robota: Radionica – Srčani sint / Heart Synth Workshop Čileanska umjetnica Constanza Piña poznata pod umjetničkim pseudonimom Corazón de Robota poziva na svoju dvodnevnu radionicu pod nazivom Srčani sint – Uzmi još jedan mali komadić mog srca koja će se održati u četvrtak i petak, 5. i 6. lipnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Nakon bezbrojnih sati popravljanja slomljenih srca tijekom svojih sesija terapije lemljenjem […] Čileanska umjetnica Constanza Piña poznata pod umjetničkim pseudonimom Corazón de Robota poziva na svoju dvodnevnu radionicu pod nazivom Srčani sint – Uzmi još jedan mali komadić mog srca koja će se održati u četvrtak i petak, 5. i 6. lipnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Nakon bezbrojnih sati popravljanja slomljenih srca tijekom svojih sesija terapije lemljenjem u Radioninom elektroničkom centru, Corazón de Robota poziva nas na radionicu gdje će podijeliti svoje stručno znanje u stvaranju malih, nestandardnih modula srca dizajniranih za generiranje buke i distorziju zvukova iz stvarnog svijeta. Naučit ćete izraditi dva modula pod nazivom “Iskrivljena ljubav” i “Ljubav kontrolirana naponom”. Kada ih međusobno povežete s trećim audio izvorom poput snimaka, instrumenata ili radija, stvorit ćete “bizaran ljubavni trokut zvuka”. To će vam omogućiti generiranje hipnotičkog zujanja, klokotavih zvukova, povremenog pucketanja, tekstura s greškama i ekstremnih distorzija. Prijavite se možete do srijede, 4. lipnja 2025. preko poveznice: https://forms.gle/d2oUTKMWvffmCuKm7 Kotizacija za radionicu iznosi 20 EUR i svoj sint nosite kući. Nakon potvrde o osiguranom mjestu na radionici, plaćanje iste obavljate na sljedeći način: – općom uplatnicom ili e-bankarstvom – pod platitelj upišite svoje podatke (ime, prezime i adresu) – pod primatelj upišite Udruga za razvoj ‘uradi sam’ kulture – Radiona, Kozjačka 41, 10 090 Zagreb, na račun: IBAN: HR2123600001102369684 – opis plaćanja: uvijek navedite naziv radionice (Radionica Srčani sint) – kopiju uplatnice donosite prvi dan radionice i predajete voditelju radionice ili šaljete na e-mail: edu.radiona.org@gmail.com – GOTOVINU NE PRIMAMO Constanza Piña , poznata i kao Corazón de Robota , umjetnica je u području sound arta i elektronike te neovisna edukatorica podrijetlom iz Curicóa u Čileu. Njezin rad temelji se na elektroničkom eksperimentiranju, tehnologijama otvorenog koda, DIY filozofiji i tehno feminističkim društvenim praksama. Istražuje buku kao zvučni, politički, kulturni i duhovni fenomen. Zanimaju je recikliranje, hakiranje hardvera, soft-circuit- ovi, DIY antene, ručni sintisajzeri, tehnologije predaka i elektronička čarobnjaštva. Constanza je aktivna na underground glazbenoj sceni od 2010. pod pseudonimom Corazón de Robota (Žensko-robotsko srce). Isključivo koristi svoje samostalno izrađene DIY sintisajzere za istraživanje područja čujnih i nečujnih frekvencija, psihofizičke percepcije zvuka i ritmičke dimenzije buke. Jedan od njezinih istaknutih projekata, „Khipu | Pre-Electrotextile Hispanic Computer“, nagrađen je na Ars Electronica Prix 2020. i reinterpretira andske sustave znanja kroz prizmu znanstvene fantastike. Sve se svodi na vraćanje i validaciju znanja koje je često marginalizirano od strane mainstream znanosti. Constanzin rad izlagan je diljem svijeta – od MOLAA u Los Angelesu do ZKM-a u Njemačkoj, Sonar+D u Španjolskoj, FILE u Brazilu, te u muzejima i kulturnim prostorima diljem Latinske Amerike, Europe, Azije i Sjeverne Amerike. Također je osnovala Cyborgrrrls (@cyborgrrrls), tehnofeminističke susrete usmjerene na izgradnju feminističkih i subverzivnih tehnoloških prostora. Danas radi samostalno kao umjetnica i edukatorica kroz svoj projekt Non Binary Electronic Berlin . Podržali: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske Grad Zagreb Zaklada Kultura nova //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// Corazón de Robota: Heart Synth Workshop Chilean artist Constanza Piña, known under the artistic pseudonym Corazón de Robota, invites you to her two-day workshop titled Heart Synth – Take Another Little Piece of My Heart , which will take place on Wednesday and Thursday, June 4th and 5th, 2025, from 6pm at Radiona.org. After countless hours mending broken hearts during her solder therapy sessions at Radiona’s electronic spiritual retreat, Corazón de Robota invites us to a workshop where she’ll share her expertise in creating small, non-standard heart modules designed to generate noise and distort sounds from the real world. You’ll learn to build two modules: “Distorted Love” and “Voltage-Controlled Love.” When you interconnect these with a third audio source like recordings, instruments, or a radio, you’ll create a “bizarre love triangle of sound”. This will allow you to generate hypnotic hums, bubbling sounds, intermittent crackles, glitchy textures, and extreme distortions. You can register by Wednesday, June 4, 2025 via the link: https://forms.gle/d2oUTKMWvffmCuKm7 The workshop fee is 20 EUR and you take your synth home. After confirming your place at the workshop, you can pay for it in the following way: – by general payment slip or e-banking – under payer, enter your details (name, surname and address) – under recipient, enter the Association for the Development of DIY Culture – Radiona, Kozjačka 41, 10 090 Zagreb, to the account: IBAN: HR2123600001102369684 – payment description: always state the name of the workshop (Radionica Srčani sint) – bring a copy of the payment slip on the first day of the workshop and hand it over to the workshop leader or send it to e-mail: edu.radiona.org@gmail.com – WE DO NOT ACCEPT CASH Constanza Piña aka Corazón de Robota is a sound electronic artist and independent educator originally from Curicó, Chile. Her work is based on electronic experimentation, open source technologies, DIY philosophy and techno feminist social practices. She explores noise as a sonic, political, cultural and spiritual phenomenon. Interested in recycling, hardware hacking, soft-circuits, DIY antennas, handicrafts synths, ancestral technologies, and electronic wizardry, Constanza is active in the underground music scene since 2010 under the pseudonym Corazón de Robota (She-Robot Heart)she exclusively uses her self-built DIY synthesizers to explore the field of audible and inaudible frequencies, the psycho-physical perceptions of sound, and the rhythmic dimensions of noise. One of her standout projects, “Khipu | Pre-Electrotextile Hispanic Computer,” was awarded at the Ars Electronica Prix 2020 and reimagines Andean knowledge systems through a science fiction lens. It’s all about reclaiming and validating knowledge that’s often sidelined by mainstream science. Constanza ’s work has been exhibited around the world—from MOLAA in Los Angeles to ZKM in Germany, Sonar+D in Spain, FILE in Brazil, and at museums and cultural spaces across Latin America, Europe, Asia, and North America. She also founded Cyborgrrrls (@cyborgrrrls), a technofeminist meeting focused on building feminist and subversive tech spaces. Today, she works independently as an artist and educator through her project Non Binary Electronic Berlin. Support: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia City of Zagreb Kultura Nova Foundation', '# Corazón de Robota: Radionica – Srčani sint / Heart Synth Workshop Čileanska umjetnica Constanza Piña poznata pod umjetničkim pseudonimom Corazón de Robota poziva na svoju dvodnevnu radionicu pod nazivom Srčani sint – Uzmi još jedan mali komadić mog srca koja će se održati u četvrtak i petak, 5. i 6. lipnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Nakon bezbrojnih sati popravljanja slomljenih srca tijekom svojih sesija terapije lemljenjem […] Čileanska umjetnica Constanza Piña poznata pod umjetničkim pseudonimom Corazón de Robota poziva na svoju dvodnevnu radionicu pod nazivom Srčani sint – Uzmi još jedan mali komadić mog srca koja će se održati u četvrtak i petak, 5. i 6. lipnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. Nakon bezbrojnih sati popravljanja slomljenih srca tijekom svojih sesija terapije lemljenjem u Radioninom elektroničkom centru, Corazón de Robota poziva nas na radionicu gdje će podijeliti svoje stručno ');
