inistarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske // Grad Zagreb // // Zaklada Kultura nova', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10819-radionica-kako-snimati-kao-profesionalac-br-3.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/radionica-kako-snimati-kao-profesionalac-br-3/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (258, 'Monika Pocrnjić – artist-in-residence', 'https://radiona.org/monika-pocrnjic-artist-in-residence/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10822-monika-pocrnjić-artist-in-residence.md', '# Monika Pocrnjić – artist-in-residence During July Monika Pocrnjić (SI) will partake our artist-in-residence program at Radiona working on her current hacking and hybrid arts projects. Monika Pocrnjić is a graduate of art education and an intermedia artist. She works in the fields of do-it-yourself (DIY) electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as […] During July Monika Pocrnjić (SI) will partake our artist-in-residence program at Radiona working on her current hacking and hybrid arts projects. Monika Pocrnjić is a graduate of art education and an intermedia artist. She works in the fields of do-it-yourself (DIY) electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as object as interface, robotic theater and the role of technologies in the modern world. In her works of art, she uses and combines various methods, media and techniques, including 3D technologies, hacking and creative coding. She displays these objects in performative events or theater performances. She lives in Ruše, works in Maribor and around the world. Supported: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske // Grad Zagreb // // Zaklada Kultura nova', '# Monika Pocrnjić – artist-in-residence During July Monika Pocrnjić (SI) will partake our artist-in-residence program at Radiona working on her current hacking and hybrid arts projects. Monika Pocrnjić is a graduate of art education and an intermedia artist. She works in the fields of do-it-yourself (DIY) electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as […] During July Monika Pocrnjić (SI) will partake our artist-in-residence program at Radiona working on her current hacking and hybrid arts projects. Monika Pocrnjić is a graduate of art education and an intermedia artist. She works in the fields of do-it-yourself (DIY) electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as object as interface, robotic theater and the role of technologies in the modern world. In her works of art, she uses and combines various methods, med');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Monika Pocrnjić – artist-in-residence', '# Monika Pocrnjić – artist-in-residence During July Monika Pocrnjić (SI) will partake our artist-in-residence program at Radiona working on her current hacking and hybrid arts projects. Monika Pocrnjić is a graduate of art education and an intermedia artist. She works in the fields of do-it-yourself (DIY) electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as […] During July Monika Pocrnjić (SI) will partake our artist-in-residence program at Radiona working on her current hacking and hybrid arts projects. Monika Pocrnjić is a graduate of art education and an intermedia artist. She works in the fields of do-it-yourself (DIY) electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as object as interface, robotic theater and the role of technologies in the modern world. In her works of art, she uses and combines various methods, media and techniques, including 3D technologies, hacking and creative coding. She displays these objects in performative events or theater performances. She lives in Ruše, works in Maribor and around the world. Supported: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske // Grad Zagreb // // Zaklada Kultura nova', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10822-monika-pocrnjić-artist-in-residence.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/monika-pocrnjic-artist-in-residence/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (259, 'DIY Lutkotronik radionica / DIY Puppet-tronics Workshop', 'https://radiona.org/diy-lutkotronik-radionica-diy-puppet-tronics-workshop/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10831-diy-lutkotronik-radionica-diy-puppet-tronics-workshop.md', '# DIY Lutkotronik radionica / DIY Puppet-tronics Workshop Radionica pod nazivom DIY Lutkotronik / DIY Puppet-tronics slovenske umjetnice Monike Pocrnjić održat će se u četvrtak, 17. srpnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. puppet-tro Lutkotronik je razigrana i praktična eksperimentalna radionica u kojoj se susreću obrt i strujni krugovi. Sudionici će izraditi vlastite lutke za prste koristeći tekstil, konac i maštu, a zatim će […] Radionica pod nazivom DIY Lutkotronik / DIY Puppet-tronics slovenske umjetnice Monike Pocrnjić održat će se u četvrtak, 17. srpnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. puppet-tro Lutkotronik je razigrana i praktična eksperimentalna radionica u kojoj se susreću obrt i strujni krugovi. Sudionici će izraditi vlastite lutke za prste koristeći tekstil, konac i maštu, a zatim će ih oživjeti ugrađenom elektronikom. Istražit ćemo šivanje vodljivim koncem, integriranje LED dioda i eksperimentiranje s mehaničkim lutkama na bazi papira i tekstila koristeći strujne krugove od bakrene trake. Nije potrebno prethodno iskustvo – samo znatiželja i spremnost za šivanje, žicu i osmišljavanje. Dođite i izradite stvorenja koja trepću, kreću se ili svijetle – pokretana vašom kreativnošću i daškom tehnologije. Prijaviti se možete preko poveznice: https://forms.gle/g2CvTWcWywVQQJxV9 do četvrtka, 17. srpnja 2025. točno u podne. Radionica je besplatna i intergeneracijska. Monika Pocrnjić studirala je likovnu kulturu i djeluje niz godina kao novomedijska umjetnica u području hibridnih umjetnosti. Radi na području uradi-sam elektronike, crtanja i kazališta lutaka. U svom radu fokusira se na pojmove kao što su objekt kao sučelje, robotsko kazalište i uloga tehnologija u modernom svijetu. U svojim umjetničkim djelima koristi i kombinira različite metode, medije i tehnike, uključujući 3D tehnologije, hakiranje i kreativno kodiranje. Te predmete kao instalacije prikazuje u performativnim događajima ili kazališnim predstavama. Živi u mjestu Ruše, radi u Mariboru i svuda po svijetu. Do sada izlagala i vodila radionice na nizu međunarodnih festivala, izložbi i događanja. Web: https://www.instagram.com/monitronica/ https://github.com/monitronica Podržali: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske, Grad Zagreb, Zaklada Kultura nova ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// The workshop titled DIY Puppet-tronics by Slovenian artist Monika Pocrnjić will be held on Thursday, July 17, 2025, at 6 pm in the Workshop. Puppet-tronics is a playful hands-on experimental workshop where craft and circuitry meet. Participants will create their own finger puppets using textiles, thread, and imagination—then bring them to life with embedded electronics. We’ll explore sewing with conductive thread, integrating LEDs, and experimenting with paper-based mechanical puppets using copper tape circuits. No prior experience needed—just curiosity and a willingness to stitch, wire, and invent. Come craft creatures that blink, move, or glow—powered by your creativity and a touch of tech.” You can register via the link: https://forms.gle/g2CvTWcWywVQQJxV9 by Thursday, July 17, 2025 at noon. The workshop is free and intergenerational. Monika Pocrnjić studied fine arts and has been working as a new media artist in the field of hybrid arts for many years. She works in the field of DIY electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as the object as an interface, robotic theatre and the role of technology in the modern world. In her artworks, she uses and combines different methods, media and techniques, including 3D technologies, hacking and creative coding. She presents these objects as installations in performative events or theatre plays. She lives in Ruše, works in Maribor and all over the world. So far, she has exhibited and led workshops at a number of international festivals, exhibitions and events. Web: https://www.instagram.com/monitronica/ https://github.com/monitronica Supported by: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia, City of Zagreb, Kultura Nova Foundation', '# DIY Lutkotronik radionica / DIY Puppet-tronics Workshop Radionica pod nazivom DIY Lutkotronik / DIY Puppet-tronics slovenske umjetnice Monike Pocrnjić održat će se u četvrtak, 17. srpnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. puppet-tro Lutkotronik je razigrana i praktična eksperimentalna radionica u kojoj se susreću obrt i strujni krugovi. Sudionici će izraditi vlastite lutke za prste koristeći tekstil, konac i maštu, a zatim će […] Radionica pod nazivom DIY Lutkotronik / DIY Puppet-tronics slovenske umjetnice Monike Pocrnjić održat će se u četvrtak, 17. srpnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. puppet-tro Lutkotronik je razigrana i praktična eksperimentalna radionica u kojoj se susreću obrt i strujni krugovi. Sudionici će izraditi vlastite lutke za prste koristeći tekstil, konac i maštu, a zatim će ih oživjeti ugrađenom elektronikom. Istražit ćemo šivanje vodljivim koncem, integriranje LED dioda i eksperiment');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('DIY Lutkotronik radionica / DIY Puppet-tronics Workshop', '# DIY Lutkotronik radionica / DIY Puppet-tronics Workshop Radionica pod nazivom DIY Lutkotronik / DIY Puppet-tronics slovenske umjetnice Monike Pocrnjić održat će se u četvrtak, 17. srpnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. puppet-tro Lutkotronik je razigrana i praktična eksperimentalna radionica u kojoj se susreću obrt i strujni krugovi. Sudionici će izraditi vlastite lutke za prste koristeći tekstil, konac i maštu, a zatim će […] Radionica pod nazivom DIY Lutkotronik / DIY Puppet-tronics slovenske umjetnice Monike Pocrnjić održat će se u četvrtak, 17. srpnja 2025. od 18h u Radioni. puppet-tro Lutkotronik je razigrana i praktična eksperimentalna radionica u kojoj se susreću obrt i strujni krugovi. Sudionici će izraditi vlastite lutke za prste koristeći tekstil, konac i maštu, a zatim će ih oživjeti ugrađenom elektronikom. Istražit ćemo šivanje vodljivim koncem, integriranje LED dioda i eksperimentiranje s mehaničkim lutkama na bazi papira i tekstila koristeći strujne krugove od bakrene trake. Nije potrebno prethodno iskustvo – samo znatiželja i spremnost za šivanje, žicu i osmišljavanje. Dođite i izradite stvorenja koja trepću, kreću se ili svijetle – pokretana vašom kreativnošću i daškom tehnologije. Prijaviti se možete preko poveznice: https://forms.gle/g2CvTWcWywVQQJxV9 do četvrtka, 17. srpnja 2025. točno u podne. Radionica je besplatna i intergeneracijska. Monika Pocrnjić studirala je likovnu kulturu i djeluje niz godina kao novomedijska umjetnica u području hibridnih umjetnosti. Radi na području uradi-sam elektronike, crtanja i kazališta lutaka. U svom radu fokusira se na pojmove kao što su objekt kao sučelje, robotsko kazalište i uloga tehnologija u modernom svijetu. U svojim umjetničkim djelima koristi i kombinira različite metode, medije i tehnike, uključujući 3D tehnologije, hakiranje i kreativno kodiranje. Te predmete kao instalacije prikazuje u performativnim događajima ili kazališnim predstavama. Živi u mjestu Ruše, radi u Mariboru i svuda po svijetu. Do sada izlagala i vodila radionice na nizu međunarodnih festivala, izložbi i događanja. Web: https://www.instagram.com/monitronica/ https://github.com/monitronica Podržali: Ministarstvo kulture i medija Republike Hrvatske, Grad Zagreb, Zaklada Kultura nova ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// The workshop titled DIY Puppet-tronics by Slovenian artist Monika Pocrnjić will be held on Thursday, July 17, 2025, at 6 pm in the Workshop. Puppet-tronics is a playful hands-on experimental workshop where craft and circuitry meet. Participants will create their own finger puppets using textiles, thread, and imagination—then bring them to life with embedded electronics. We’ll explore sewing with conductive thread, integrating LEDs, and experimenting with paper-based mechanical puppets using copper tape circuits. No prior experience needed—just curiosity and a willingness to stitch, wire, and invent. Come craft creatures that blink, move, or glow—powered by your creativity and a touch of tech.” You can register via the link: https://forms.gle/g2CvTWcWywVQQJxV9 by Thursday, July 17, 2025 at noon. The workshop is free and intergenerational. Monika Pocrnjić studied fine arts and has been working as a new media artist in the field of hybrid arts for many years. She works in the field of DIY electronics, drawing and puppet theatre. In her work, she focuses on concepts such as the object as an interface, robotic theatre and the role of technology in the modern world. In her artworks, she uses and combines different methods, media and techniques, including 3D technologies, hacking and creative coding. She presents these objects as installations in performative events or theatre plays. She lives in Ruše, works in Maribor and all over the world. So far, she has exhibited and led workshops at a number of international festivals, exhibitions and events. Web: https://www.instagram.com/monitronica/ https://github.com/monitronica Supported by: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia, City of Zagreb, Kultura Nova Foundation', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-10831-diy-lutkotronik-radionica-diy-puppet-tronics-workshop.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/diy-lutkotronik-radionica-diy-puppet-tronics-workshop/');
