asco.gram (cc) In a world that produces faster than it can think, upcycling emerges as a silent but decisive gesture of resistance. Instead of new fabric, we choose an existing one; instead of discarding, transformation. Upcycling is not just a method, but a way to slow down the pace of hyperproduction and re-establish a relationship with the material. In the workshop, we will work with blankets – objects of warmth, memory and durability – and transform them into garments: jackets, skirts and other wearable forms. Through cutting, combining and reinventing, the blanket becomes a garment, and the garment becomes a new story. Participants should bring an old blanket that they no longer use and an old piece of clothing to combine (such as a hoodie, sweater, jacket or similar piece). The workshop is open to anyone who wants to think about fashion beyond the logic of the new, the seasonal and the surplus – and give new life to the material with their own hands. You can register at the link: https://shorturl.at/6yJH0 by Friday, January 23, 2025 at noon. The registration fee is 15.00 EUR. Due to the complexity of the use of industrial machines, the workshop has been moved to Vasco’s studio with a maximum of 7 participants. After confirming your place at the workshop, you can pay for it in the following way: – by general payment slip or e-banking – under payer, enter your details (name, surname and address) – under recipient, enter the Association for the Development of DIY Culture – Radiona, Kozjačka 41, 10 090 Zagreb, to the account: IBAN: HR2123600001102369684 – payment description: always state the name of the workshop (Sewing workshop: blanket) – bring a copy of the payment slip on the first day of the workshop and hand it over to the workshop leader or send it to e-mail: edu.radiona.org@gmail.com – WE DO NOT ACCEPT CASH About the workshop leader: Vasco (instagram.com/vasco.gram) – Vasco is a textile and fashion slager based in Zagreb, owner of the eponymous craft founded in 2022. His works are often provocative and daring, designed to encourage reflection and conversation about important social topics. He considers fashion a place of mass enslavement, but also personal emancipation. He has been collaborating with various actors on the cultural and artistic scene for many years. Graduated from the Faculty of Textile Technology, Textile and Fashion Design, Textile Design in 2022. In the last few years, he has exhibited individually or in groups and held workshops at the Nikola Tesla Technical Museum, the 55th Zagreb Salon, Zagreb Design Week, the Museum of Arts and Crafts, the Q Fest festival, and through various projects he has collaborated with Sabmarine, the Academy of Dramatic Arts, etc., and is now working on films and commercials in the costume design sector. He passes on his knowledge through workshops and private lessons. He is a long-time collaborator of Radiona, within whose educational program he works on the textile program. Supported by: Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia // Kultura Nova Foundation', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11088-radionica-šivanja-ispod-deke-u-jaknu-sewing-workshop-from-under-the-blanket-into-a-jacket.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/radionica-sivanja-ispod-deke-u-jaknu-sewing-workshop-from-under-the-blanket-into-a-jacket/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (285, 'Ableton sesije s Paulom / Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona', 'https://radiona.org/ableton-sesije-s-paulom-ableton-sessions-with-paul-radiona/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11101-ableton-sesije-s-paulom-ableton-sessions-with-paul-radiona.md', '# Ableton sesije s Paulom / Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona Paul Grandjean poziva sve zainteresirane za glazbenu produkciju na svoje sesije u Radioni. Ove su sesije namijenjene istraživanju načinima na koji želite stvarati glazbu, bilo da je to techno, ambient, eksperimentalna mjuza ili nešto drugo. Ableton je samo alat — pravi fokus sesija ste vi i vaš zvuk. Photo by Erwi on Unsplash (cc) Za […] Paul Grandjean poziva sve zainteresirane za glazbenu produkciju na svoje sesije u Radioni. Ove su sesije namijenjene istraživanju načinima na koji želite stvarati glazbu, bilo da je to techno, ambient, eksperimentalna mjuza ili nešto drugo. Ableton je samo alat — pravi fokus sesija ste vi i vaš zvuk. Photo by Erwi on Unsplash (cc) Za prijavu potrebno je imati popis od 5 pjesama koje vas predstavljaju + 5 žanrova/vrsta glazbe koju biste željeli stvoriti. Nakon što proučim vaše interese, stvaram lekcije usmjerene na vas. Na sesijama ćemo prolaziti područja od uzorkovanja i sinteze do dizajna zvuka i resampliranja, koristeći alate poput Samplera, Simplera, Operatora, Analog, Collisiona i nekoliko mojih omiljenih dodataka – pluginova , trikova i kreativnih tijekova rada ( workflow ). Naučit ćete kako izgraditi vlastitu zvučnu biblioteku, oblikovati teksture i, što je najvažnije, kako stvarno slušati ono što stvarate. Grupe su male, tako da svatko dobiva vrijeme, prostor i vodstvo za vlastiti stil i tempo. I za početak — nudim besplatni uvodni tečaj od 2 sata za upoznavanje, sviranje i dobivanje uvida u ono što tečaj nudi. Dođite istraživati, stvarati buku i pronaći svoj zvuk. Što je potrebno: •⁠ ⁠Laptop •⁠ ⁠slušalice •⁠ ⁠Motivacija Prijaviti se možete preko poveznice: https://forms.gle/j7gTk3CErP8sYYVM9 A možete i prethodno kontaktirati voditelja imate neka pitanja – WhatsApp: 0033685898303; adiktivist @ gmail . com Radni jezik je primarno engleski. O voditelju: Paul Grandjean (Genetik Dub) rodio se u Parizu, a u Hrvatskoj živi posljednjih desetak godina. Više od dvadeset godina stvara elektroničku glazbu na Abletonu (dub, techno, postrock, IDM, breakcore…). Surađuje s različitim umjetnicima koji poboljšavaju njegovu percepciju glazbenog spektra i nagnali su ga da shvati da postoji beskonačno mnogo načina stvaranja i eksperimentiranja s glazbom. Osim toga, bavi se izradom scenografije i namještaja u domaćem i inozemnom kontekstu. //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona These sessions are about exploring how to create the kind of music you want to make, whether it’s techno, ambient, experimental, or something else. Ableton is just the tool — the real focus is you and your sound. I ask a playlist of 5 tracks that represent you + 5 of the music you d like to create. I’m studying it and then make lessons focused on you. We’ll go from sampling and synthesis to sound design and resampling, using tools like Sampler, Simpler, Operator, Analog, Collision and a few of my favorite plugins, tricks, and creative workflows. You’ll learn how to build your own sound library, shape textures, and most importantly, how to really listen to what you’re creating. Groups are kept small, so everyone gets time, space, and guidance for their own style and pace. And to kick things off — I’m offering a free 2-hours intro class to meet, jam, and get a taste of what the course is all about. Come explore, make noise, and find your sound. What is needed : •⁠ ⁠Laptop •⁠ ⁠headphones •⁠ ⁠Motivation Prijavite se putem poveznice: https://forms.gle/j7gTk3CErP8sYYVM9 A možete i prethodno kontaktirati voditelja imate neka pitanja – WhatsApp: 0033685898303; adiktivist @ gmail . com The working language is primarily English. About the mentor: Paul Grandjean (Genetik Dub) is a native of Paris, living in Croatia for the past ten years. He has been creating electronic music on Ableton for more than twenty years (dub, techno, postrock, IDM, breakcore…). He collaborates with various artists who improve his perception of the musical spectrum and have made him realize that there are infinitely many ways to create and experiment with music. In addition, he is engaged in the creation of scenography and furniture in domestic and international contexts.', '# Ableton sesije s Paulom / Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona Paul Grandjean poziva sve zainteresirane za glazbenu produkciju na svoje sesije u Radioni. Ove su sesije namijenjene istraživanju načinima na koji želite stvarati glazbu, bilo da je to techno, ambient, eksperimentalna mjuza ili nešto drugo. Ableton je samo alat — pravi fokus sesija ste vi i vaš zvuk. Photo by Erwi on Unsplash (cc) Za […] Paul Grandjean poziva sve zainteresirane za glazbenu produkciju na svoje sesije u Radioni. Ove su sesije namijenjene istraživanju načinima na koji želite stvarati glazbu, bilo da je to techno, ambient, eksperimentalna mjuza ili nešto drugo. Ableton je samo alat — pravi fokus sesija ste vi i vaš zvuk. Photo by Erwi on Unsplash (cc) Za prijavu potrebno je imati popis od 5 pjesama koje vas predstavljaju + 5 žanrova/vrsta glazbe koju biste željeli stvoriti. Nakon što proučim vaše interese, stva');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Ableton sesije s Paulom / Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona', '# Ableton sesije s Paulom / Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona Paul Grandjean poziva sve zainteresirane za glazbenu produkciju na svoje sesije u Radioni. Ove su sesije namijenjene istraživanju načinima na koji želite stvarati glazbu, bilo da je to techno, ambient, eksperimentalna mjuza ili nešto drugo. Ableton je samo alat — pravi fokus sesija ste vi i vaš zvuk. Photo by Erwi on Unsplash (cc) Za […] Paul Grandjean poziva sve zainteresirane za glazbenu produkciju na svoje sesije u Radioni. Ove su sesije namijenjene istraživanju načinima na koji želite stvarati glazbu, bilo da je to techno, ambient, eksperimentalna mjuza ili nešto drugo. Ableton je samo alat — pravi fokus sesija ste vi i vaš zvuk. Photo by Erwi on Unsplash (cc) Za prijavu potrebno je imati popis od 5 pjesama koje vas predstavljaju + 5 žanrova/vrsta glazbe koju biste željeli stvoriti. Nakon što proučim vaše interese, stvaram lekcije usmjerene na vas. Na sesijama ćemo prolaziti područja od uzorkovanja i sinteze do dizajna zvuka i resampliranja, koristeći alate poput Samplera, Simplera, Operatora, Analog, Collisiona i nekoliko mojih omiljenih dodataka – pluginova , trikova i kreativnih tijekova rada ( workflow ). Naučit ćete kako izgraditi vlastitu zvučnu biblioteku, oblikovati teksture i, što je najvažnije, kako stvarno slušati ono što stvarate. Grupe su male, tako da svatko dobiva vrijeme, prostor i vodstvo za vlastiti stil i tempo. I za početak — nudim besplatni uvodni tečaj od 2 sata za upoznavanje, sviranje i dobivanje uvida u ono što tečaj nudi. Dođite istraživati, stvarati buku i pronaći svoj zvuk. Što je potrebno: •⁠ ⁠Laptop •⁠ ⁠slušalice •⁠ ⁠Motivacija Prijaviti se možete preko poveznice: https://forms.gle/j7gTk3CErP8sYYVM9 A možete i prethodno kontaktirati voditelja imate neka pitanja – WhatsApp: 0033685898303; adiktivist @ gmail . com Radni jezik je primarno engleski. O voditelju: Paul Grandjean (Genetik Dub) rodio se u Parizu, a u Hrvatskoj živi posljednjih desetak godina. Više od dvadeset godina stvara elektroničku glazbu na Abletonu (dub, techno, postrock, IDM, breakcore…). Surađuje s različitim umjetnicima koji poboljšavaju njegovu percepciju glazbenog spektra i nagnali su ga da shvati da postoji beskonačno mnogo načina stvaranja i eksperimentiranja s glazbom. Osim toga, bavi se izradom scenografije i namještaja u domaćem i inozemnom kontekstu. //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// Ableton Sessions with Paul @ Radiona These sessions are about exploring how to create the kind of music you want to make, whether it’s techno, ambient, experimental, or something else. Ableton is just the tool — the real focus is you and your sound. I ask a playlist of 5 tracks that represent you + 5 of the music you d like to create. I’m studying it and then make lessons focused on you. We’ll go from sampling and synthesis to sound design and resampling, using tools like Sampler, Simpler, Operator, Analog, Collision and a few of my favorite plugins, tricks, and creative workflows. You’ll learn how to build your own sound library, shape textures, and most importantly, how to really listen to what you’re creating. Groups are kept small, so everyone gets time, space, and guidance for their own style and pace. And to kick things off — I’m offering a free 2-hours intro class to meet, jam, and get a taste of what the course is all about. Come explore, make noise, and find your sound. What is needed : •⁠ ⁠Laptop •⁠ ⁠headphones •⁠ ⁠Motivation Prijavite se putem poveznice: https://forms.gle/j7gTk3CErP8sYYVM9 A možete i prethodno kontaktirati voditelja imate neka pitanja – WhatsApp: 0033685898303; adiktivist @ gmail . com The working language is primarily English. About the mentor: Paul Grandjean (Genetik Dub) is a native of Paris, living in Croatia for the past ten years. He has been creating electronic music on Ableton for more than twenty years (dub, techno, postrock, IDM, breakcore…). He collaborates with various artists who improve his perception of the musical spectrum and have made him realize that there are infinitely many ways to create and experiment with music. In addition, he is engaged in the creation of scenography and furniture in domestic and international contexts.', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11101-ableton-sesije-s-paulom-ableton-sessions-with-paul-radiona.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/ableton-sesije-s-paulom-ableton-sessions-with-paul-radiona/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (286, 'Radionica Synthomir / Workshop', 'https://radiona.org/radionica-synthomir-workshop/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11107-radionica-synthomir-workshop.md', '# Radionica Synthomir / Workshop U sklopu obilježavanja dvanaest godina od nastanka prvog Radioninog sintesajzera – Synthomira, održat će se istoimena radionica pod vodstvom Igora Brkića, u subotu 24. siječnja 2026. godine, od 15:00 do 19:00 sati u prostoru Radione. For English please scroll down. Synthomir GIF: Damir Prizmić , Radiona.org (cc) Synthomir je 8-bitni DIY sintesajzer temeljen na ATmega […] U sklopu obilježavanja dvanaest godina od nastanka prvog Radioninog sintesajzera – Synthomira, održat će se istoimena radionica pod vodstvom Igora Brkića, u subotu 24. siječnja 2026. godine, od 15:00 do 19:00 sati u prostoru Radione. For English please scroll down. Synthomir GIF: Damir Prizmić , Radiona.org (cc) Synthomir je 8-bitni DIY sintesajzer temeljen na ATmega mikrokontroleru, kompatibilan s Arduino razvojnim okruženjem, koji za sintezu zvuka koristi Mozzi library. Omogućuje tri načina rada – ritam mašinu (s loop modom), bas i teremin mode – dok se njegovo minimalističko korisničko sučelje sastoji od samo tri elementa: potenciometra, fotootpornika i tipkala. Takav reducirani pristup osmišljen je kako bi poticao eksperimentiranje te omogućio buduće nadogradnje i modifikacije. (Detaljnije o tome kako je krenuo Synthomir pročitajte na dnu teksta) Ako želite svoj primjerak sada već kultnog sintesajzera koji možete dodatno sami dalje razvijati, vrijeme je da se bacite u to prije nego DIY kitovi nestanu. Prijaviti se možete preko poveznice: https://forms.gle/Ld7kDHighAoHvBW36 do četvrtka, 22. siječnja 2026. u ponoć. Kotizacija za Synthomir iznosi 40.00 EUR i nosite svoj uređaj kući (podatke za uplatu dobijete nakon prijave). O voditelju: Igor Brkić diplomirao je na Fakultetu elektrotehnike i računarstva gdje se bavio digitalnom obradom audio signala. Bavi se embedded i web programiranjem, dizajnom elektroničkih uređaja i glazbom. Sudjelovao je na brojnim izložbama i projektima te je već niz godina voditelj uspješnih radionica s posebnim fokusom na Arduino, kreativnu upotrebu senzora u interaktivnim instalacijama, sintezu zvuka, 3D modeliranje u FreeCAD-u, izrada PCB-a u KiCAD-u, kriptografija i privatnost, dizajn i programiranje e-bedževa. Autor je mnogih robotičkih i elektroničkih rješenja za muzejske kuće, izložbe, domaće i međunarodne kazališne predstave, televizijske emisije i samostalne umjetnike. Svoje interaktivne radove redovito izlaže u sklopu Radioninog izlagačkog programa čiji je jedan od su-osnivača, dok je međunarodno etabliran u okviru Hackaday zajednice u sklopu koje redovito objavljuje svoje open source projekte i hakaže uređaja. Posebno treba istaknuti njegov doprinos razvoju e-bedževa za konferenciju DORS/CLUC koji su predstavljeni na nizu regionalnih open source i hakerskim konferencijama. U sklopu međunarodnog projekta Kreativni muzej bio je dobitnik 10dnevne rezidencije za makere u Norveškoj. Svojim start-upom Hyperglitch djeluje sad već niz godina u vodećim međunarodnim ICT projektima. Web: hyperglitch.com Kako je krenuo Synthomir? Synthomir je zamišljen kao DIY elektronički komplet za slaganje i dio je istraživanja ‘Amplitude slike i zvuka’ koje je Radiona – Udruga za razvoj „uradi sam“ kulture provodila tijekom 2014. godine, uz potporu Zaklade Kultura nova. Riječ je ujedno o prvoj institucionalnoj podršci udruzi nakon njezina formalnog osnivanja. Projekt je u potpunosti open source – izvorni kod, elektronička shema i datoteke za izradu pločica slobodno su dostupni za korištenje, prilagodbu i daljnji razvoj. Elektroničku shemu i zvučni koncept Synthomira razvio je Igor Brkić, dizajn pločice i vizualni koncept potpisuje Damir Prizmić, dok je Deborah Hustić osmislila istraživački okvir projekta i ime sintesajzera. Od svog nastanka, Synthomir je prepoznat i izvan DIY i makerske zajednice. 2016. godine Synthomir je bio izložen na Venecijanskom bijenalu arhitekture u sklopu hrvatskog nastupa te je iste godine dobio posebno priznanje u profesionalnoj selekciji kategorije produkt dizajna Hrvatskog dizajnerskog društva, u sklopu bijenalne Izložbe hrvatskog dizajna. Predstavljen je također na EarZoom Sonic Arts Festival / Music Tech Fest-u u Ljubljani. Od radionica izdvajamo održavanje iste u sklopu Device_arta 5.015 u Zagrebu, događanja Cirkulacija2 et al. Access to Tools kod Cirkulacije2 i Aksiome u Ljubljani, u sklopu KLFM programa ‘Radio dan i noć’ u suradnji s UMAS-om u Splitu te na simpoziju Creative Museum u Bologni. Izlagan je na nizu izložbi od kojih izdvajamo ZEZ Festival, festival Napusti normalne naprave Drugog mora u Rijeci, međunarodna izložba WonderLab u Muzeju savremene umetnosti Vojvodine u Novom Sadu, Radioninoj izložbi Zvučni hibridi ­- kreativna sonologija u Tehničkom muzeju Nikola Tesla, Maker Faire Ljubljana, Maker Faire Trondheim. U 2024. godini produkciju Synthomira preuzima start-up Intergalaktik iz Zagreba. ////////////////////////////////////////////////// As part of the celebration marking twelve years since the creation of Radiona’s first synthesizer – Synthomir, a workshop of the same name will be held under the guidance of Igor Brkić on Saturday, January 24, 2026, from 3:00 PM to 7:00 PM, at Radiona. Synthomir is an 8-bit DIY synthesizer based on an ATmega microcontroller, compatible with the Arduino development environment, and using the Mozzi library for sound synthesis. It features three operating modes – a rhythm machine (with loop mode), bass, and theremin mode – while its minimalist user interface consists of only three elements: a potentiometer, a photoresistor, and a push button. This reduced approach was designed to encourage experimentation and enable future upgrades and modifications. (More details about how Synthomir began can be found at the end of the text.) If you would like your own copy of this now already cult synthesizer, which you can further develop on your own, now is the time to get started before the DIY kits run out. You can register via the following link: https://forms.gle/Ld7kDHighAoHvBW36 Registration is open until Thursday, January 22, 2026, at midnight . The participation fee for Synthomir is EUR 40.00 , and you take your device home with you. About the workshop leader: Igor Brkić graduated from the Faculty of Electrical Engineering and Computing, where he focused on digital audio signal processing. He works in embedded and web programming, electronic device design, and music. He has participated in numerous exhibitions and projects and has been leading successful workshops for many years, with a special focus on Arduino, creative use of sensors in interactive installations, sound synthesis, 3D modeling in FreeCAD, PCB design in KiCAD, cryptography and privacy, and the design and programming of e-badges. He is the author of many robotic and electronic solutions for museums, exhibitions, domestic and international theatre productions, television shows, and independent artists. He regularly exhibits his interactive works as part of Radiona’s exhibition program, of which he is one of the co-founders, and is internationally established within the Hackaday community, where he regularly publishes his open source projects and hardware hacks. His contribution to the development of e-badges for the DORS/CLUC conference, which have been presented at numerous regional open source and hacker conferences, should be particularly highlighted. As part of the international project Creative Museum , he was awarded a 10-day maker residency in Norway. Through his startup Hyperglitch , he has been active for several years in leading international ICT projects. Web: hyperglitch.com How did Synthomir begin? Synthomir was conceived as a DIY electronic kit for assembly and as part of the research project Amplitude of Image and Sound , which Radiona – the Association for the Development of “Do-It-Yourself” Culture – conducted during 2014, with the support of the Kultura Nova Foundation. This was also the first institutional support the association received after its formal founding. The project is fully open source – the source code, electronic schematics, and PCB design files are freely available for use, adaptation, and further development. The electronic schematic and sound concept of Synthomir were developed by Igor Brkić, the PCB design and visual concept were created by Damir Prizmić, while Deborah Hustić conceived the research framework of the project and the name of the synthesizer. Since its inception, Synthomir has been recognized beyond the DIY and makerspace community. In 2016, Synthomir was exhibited at the Venice Architecture Biennale as part of the Croatian national presentation, and in the same year received a Special Mention in the professional selection of the Product Design category by the Croatian Designers Association, within the Croatian Design Exhibition Biennial. It was also presented at the EarZoom Sonic Arts Festival / Music Tech Fest in Ljubljana. Among the workshops and presentations, we highlight its inclusion in Device_art 5.015 in Zagreb, the event Cirkulacija2 et al. Access to Tools organized by Cirkulacija2 and Aksioma in Ljubljana, the KLFM program Radio Day and Night in collaboration with UMAS in Split, and the Creative Museum symposium in Bologna. Synthomir has been exhibited at numerous exhibitions, including ZEZ Festival, Festival Abandon Normal Devices at Drugo more in Rijeka, the international exhibition WonderLab at the Museum of Contemporary Art of Vojvodina in Novi Sad, Radiona’s exhibition Sound Hybrids – Creative Sonology at the Nikola Tesla Technical Museum, Maker Faire Ljubljana, and Maker Faire Trondheim. In 2024 , the production of Synthomir was taken over by the Zagreb-based startup Intergalaktik . Podržali/Supported by: Zaklada Kultura nova, Ministarstvo kulture i medija RH', '# Radionica Synthomir / Workshop U sklopu obilježavanja dvanaest godina od nastanka prvog Radioninog sintesajzera – Synthomira, održat će se istoimena radionica pod vodstvom Igora Brkića, u subotu 24. siječnja 2026. godine, od 15:00 do 19:00 sati u prostoru Radione. For English please scroll down. Synthomir GIF: Damir Prizmić , Radiona.org (cc) Synthomir je 8-bitni DIY sintesajzer temeljen na ATmega […] U sklopu obilježavanja dvanaest godina od nastanka prvog Radioninog sintesajzera – Synthomira, održat će se istoimena radionica pod vodstvom Igora Brkića, u subotu 24. siječnja 2026. godine, od 15:00 do 19:00 sati u prostoru Radione. For English please scroll down. Synthomir GIF: Damir Prizmić , Radiona.org (cc) Synthomir je 8-bitni DIY sintesajzer temeljen na ATmega mikrokontroleru, kompatibilan s Arduino razvojnim okruženjem, koji za sintezu zvuka koristi Mozzi library. Omogućuje tri na');
