 Zoe Romano has a master’s degree in philosophy and media science and technology. Romano is an artist, lecturer and consultant working on EU-supported projects that combine social ecology, digital manufacturing technologies and smart fabrics. Also, she worked for several years in strategic communication, developing her social skills as a media hacktivist in the field of precariousness and tangible and intangible work in creative industries. She developed her skills in hackerspaces and makerspaces in Milan, and while working for Arduino, she co-founded fablab WeMake, focused on fashion and design. She has activated various art projects such as Obot (Our bodies our Tech) in 2020, Melma Crew in 2022, and lately she likes to spend time at art residencies and camps in Italy and abroad. Participates in research/activist initiatives and develops projects related to e-textiles and digital fabrication in different contexts. Web: www.zoeromano.eu Supported by: City of Zagreb, Ministry of Culture and Media of the Republic of Croatia, Kultura nova Foundation', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11219-zoe-romano-radionica-izrade-mekih-senzora-crafting-soft-sensors-workshop.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/zoe-romano-radionica-izrade-mekih-senzora-crafting-soft-sensors-workshop/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (294, 'FPGA ULX4M-LM to be part of Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs workshop', 'https://radiona.org/fpga-ulx4m-lm/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11231-fpga-ulx4m-lm-to-be-part-of-exploring-every-way-to-build-lattice-ecp5-fpgas-workshop.md', '# FPGA ULX4M-LM to be part of Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs workshop The ULX4M FPGA board, developed by Intergalaktik Ltd. as a continuation of the successful series of FPGA boards created within the Radiona.org – Zagreb Makerspace, and shaped through long-term open-hardware work and community collaboration, is featured as part of the online talk and workshop “Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs” by Andrew Elbert […] The ULX4M FPGA board, developed by Intergalaktik Ltd. as a continuation of the successful series of FPGA boards created within the Radiona.org – Zagreb Makerspace, and shaped through long-term open-hardware work and community collaboration, is featured as part of the online talk and workshop “Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs” by Andrew Elbert Wilson . This online talk and workshop explores multiple approaches to designing and working with Lattice ECP5 FPGA devices, with a strong focus on open-source toolchains, workflows, and hardware platforms. The latest version of the ULX4M board is used as a reference hardware platform for practical demonstrations and real-world examples throughout the session. ULX4M’s inclusion in this event highlights its relevance within the global open-source FPGA ecosystem and emphasizes the importance of locally developed knowledge and infrastructure that, through Radiona, contributes to international educational and technological initiatives. The talk and workshop take place online on February 24, 2026 with the live stream and recording available via YouTube Live: https://www.youtube.com/live/7Havv4TaeOE <span data-mce-type="bookmark" style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; overflow: hidden; line-height: 0;" class="mce_SELRES_start">﻿</span> Andrew Elbert Wilson is an FPGA engineer and educator with a strong focus on open-source hardware and toolchains. He is actively involved in developing, documenting, and teaching practical workflows for FPGA design, particularly around Lattice ECP5 devices, and regularly shares his knowledge through talks, workshops, and community-driven projects.', '# FPGA ULX4M-LM to be part of Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs workshop The ULX4M FPGA board, developed by Intergalaktik Ltd. as a continuation of the successful series of FPGA boards created within the Radiona.org – Zagreb Makerspace, and shaped through long-term open-hardware work and community collaboration, is featured as part of the online talk and workshop “Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs” by Andrew Elbert […] The ULX4M FPGA board, developed by Intergalaktik Ltd. as a continuation of the successful series of FPGA boards created within the Radiona.org – Zagreb Makerspace, and shaped through long-term open-hardware work and community collaboration, is featured as part of the online talk and workshop “Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs” by Andrew Elbert Wilson . This online talk and workshop explores multiple approaches to designing and work');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('FPGA ULX4M-LM to be part of Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs workshop', '# FPGA ULX4M-LM to be part of Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs workshop The ULX4M FPGA board, developed by Intergalaktik Ltd. as a continuation of the successful series of FPGA boards created within the Radiona.org – Zagreb Makerspace, and shaped through long-term open-hardware work and community collaboration, is featured as part of the online talk and workshop “Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs” by Andrew Elbert […] The ULX4M FPGA board, developed by Intergalaktik Ltd. as a continuation of the successful series of FPGA boards created within the Radiona.org – Zagreb Makerspace, and shaped through long-term open-hardware work and community collaboration, is featured as part of the online talk and workshop “Exploring Every Way to Build Lattice ECP5 FPGAs” by Andrew Elbert Wilson . This online talk and workshop explores multiple approaches to designing and working with Lattice ECP5 FPGA devices, with a strong focus on open-source toolchains, workflows, and hardware platforms. The latest version of the ULX4M board is used as a reference hardware platform for practical demonstrations and real-world examples throughout the session. ULX4M’s inclusion in this event highlights its relevance within the global open-source FPGA ecosystem and emphasizes the importance of locally developed knowledge and infrastructure that, through Radiona, contributes to international educational and technological initiatives. The talk and workshop take place online on February 24, 2026 with the live stream and recording available via YouTube Live: https://www.youtube.com/live/7Havv4TaeOE <span data-mce-type="bookmark" style="display: inline-block; width: 0px; overflow: hidden; line-height: 0;" class="mce_SELRES_start">﻿</span> Andrew Elbert Wilson is an FPGA engineer and educator with a strong focus on open-source hardware and toolchains. He is actively involved in developing, documenting, and teaching practical workflows for FPGA design, particularly around Lattice ECP5 devices, and regularly shares his knowledge through talks, workshops, and community-driven projects.', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11231-fpga-ulx4m-lm-to-be-part-of-exploring-every-way-to-build-lattice-ecp5-fpgas-workshop.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/fpga-ulx4m-lm/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (295, 'Radionice Elektro-diorama i Theremin Postcard u Muzeju grada Koprivnice', 'https://radiona.org/radionice-elektro-diorama-i-theremin-postcard-u-muzeju-grada-koprivnice/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11242-radionice-elektro-diorama-i-theremin-postcard-u-muzeju-grada-koprivnice.md', '# Radionice Elektro-diorama i Theremin Postcard u Muzeju grada Koprivnice Povodom završetka naše izložbe „Katalog elektro-entiteta K/3” u Muzeju grada Koprivnice u petak 6. ožujka 2026. s početkom u 11h održat ćemo dvije radionice za djecu. Za prijave molimo kontaktirati muzej. Radionica Elektro-diorama, 12+ Voditeljica: Paula Bučar Na radionici će polaznici izrađivati svjetlosne objekte – diorame koje će osvijetliti LED diodama. Diorame će se izrađivati od papira […] Povodom završetka naše izložbe „Katalog elektro-entiteta K/3” u Muzeju grada Koprivnice u petak 6. ožujka 2026. s početkom u 11h održat ćemo dvije radionice za djecu. Za prijave molimo kontaktirati muzej. Radionica Elektro-diorama, 12+ Voditeljica: Paula Bučar Na radionici će polaznici izrađivati svjetlosne objekte – diorame koje će osvijetliti LED diodama. Diorame će se izrađivati od papira prema dizajnu polaznika. Diorama izgleda poput kazališne kutije čiji se prizor sastoji od niza planova, odnosno slojeva izrezanih silueta koje stvaraju iluziju dubine. Efekti koje je moguće postići dodajući više slojeva i 3D efekt su fascinantni te je moguća primjena navedenih vještina pri stvaranju umjetnosti svjetlosnih objekata ili animiranih i eksperimentalnih filmova. Polaznici svoje radove nose kući! Radionica Theremin Postcard, 8+ Voditeljica: Deborah Hustić Teremin je glazbeni instrument koji se svira pokretom. Izumljen 1928. godine te je od tada strašno zanimljiv svim eksperimentatorima zvuka. Na ovoj radionici sudionici će naučiti kako napraviti DIY teremin čije se glasanje i zujanje modulira preko foto-senzora, a radionica je prava prilika da sudionici s jako malo elektronskih komponenti ponesu kući svoju mini varijantu teremina u obliku razglednice. Polaznici svoje radove nose kući!', '# Radionice Elektro-diorama i Theremin Postcard u Muzeju grada Koprivnice Povodom završetka naše izložbe „Katalog elektro-entiteta K/3” u Muzeju grada Koprivnice u petak 6. ožujka 2026. s početkom u 11h održat ćemo dvije radionice za djecu. Za prijave molimo kontaktirati muzej. Radionica Elektro-diorama, 12+ Voditeljica: Paula Bučar Na radionici će polaznici izrađivati svjetlosne objekte – diorame koje će osvijetliti LED diodama. Diorame će se izrađivati od papira […] Povodom završetka naše izložbe „Katalog elektro-entiteta K/3” u Muzeju grada Koprivnice u petak 6. ožujka 2026. s početkom u 11h održat ćemo dvije radionice za djecu. Za prijave molimo kontaktirati muzej. Radionica Elektro-diorama, 12+ Voditeljica: Paula Bučar Na radionici će polaznici izrađivati svjetlosne objekte – diorame koje će osvijetliti LED diodama. Diorame će se izrađivati od papira prema dizajnu polaznika. Diorama');
INSERT INTO source_chunks_fts(title, body, path, source_family, url) VALUES ('Radionice Elektro-diorama i Theremin Postcard u Muzeju grada Koprivnice', '# Radionice Elektro-diorama i Theremin Postcard u Muzeju grada Koprivnice Povodom završetka naše izložbe „Katalog elektro-entiteta K/3” u Muzeju grada Koprivnice u petak 6. ožujka 2026. s početkom u 11h održat ćemo dvije radionice za djecu. Za prijave molimo kontaktirati muzej. Radionica Elektro-diorama, 12+ Voditeljica: Paula Bučar Na radionici će polaznici izrađivati svjetlosne objekte – diorame koje će osvijetliti LED diodama. Diorame će se izrađivati od papira […] Povodom završetka naše izložbe „Katalog elektro-entiteta K/3” u Muzeju grada Koprivnice u petak 6. ožujka 2026. s početkom u 11h održat ćemo dvije radionice za djecu. Za prijave molimo kontaktirati muzej. Radionica Elektro-diorama, 12+ Voditeljica: Paula Bučar Na radionici će polaznici izrađivati svjetlosne objekte – diorame koje će osvijetliti LED diodama. Diorame će se izrađivati od papira prema dizajnu polaznika. Diorama izgleda poput kazališne kutije čiji se prizor sastoji od niza planova, odnosno slojeva izrezanih silueta koje stvaraju iluziju dubine. Efekti koje je moguće postići dodajući više slojeva i 3D efekt su fascinantni te je moguća primjena navedenih vještina pri stvaranju umjetnosti svjetlosnih objekata ili animiranih i eksperimentalnih filmova. Polaznici svoje radove nose kući! Radionica Theremin Postcard, 8+ Voditeljica: Deborah Hustić Teremin je glazbeni instrument koji se svira pokretom. Izumljen 1928. godine te je od tada strašno zanimljiv svim eksperimentatorima zvuka. Na ovoj radionici sudionici će naučiti kako napraviti DIY teremin čije se glasanje i zujanje modulira preko foto-senzora, a radionica je prava prilika da sudionici s jako malo elektronskih komponenti ponesu kući svoju mini varijantu teremina u obliku razglednice. Polaznici svoje radove nose kući!', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11242-radionice-elektro-diorama-i-theremin-postcard-u-muzeju-grada-koprivnice.md', 'radiona', 'https://radiona.org/radionice-elektro-diorama-i-theremin-postcard-u-muzeju-grada-koprivnice/');
INSERT INTO source_chunks(id, title, url, source_family, path, body, description) VALUES (296, 'eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corner @ BSides Zagreb 2026', 'https://radiona.org/ebadge-zigzag-i-neoretro-corner-bsides-zagreb-2026/', 'radiona', 'Sources/Raw/radiona/post-11247-ebadge-zigzag-i-neoretro-corner-bsides-zagreb-2026.md', '# eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corner @ BSides Zagreb 2026 Radionin program eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corner sudjeluje u programu međunarodne BSides Zagreb 2026 konferencije u Zagrebu koja se održava 6. ožujka 2026. Radionu će predstavljati Goran Mahovlić, Emard, Vlado Vince i dr. ZigZag eBadge razvili Goran Mahovlić (hardware) i Damir Prizmić (dizajn). NeoRetro Corner izložbena je selekcija neo i retro tehnologija iz Radionine kolekcije […] Radionin program eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corne r sudjeluje u programu međunarodne BSides Zagreb 2026 konferencije u Zagrebu koja se održava 6. ožujka 2026. Radionu će predstavljati Goran Mahovlić, Emard, Vlado Vince i dr. ZigZag eBadge razvili Goran Mahovlić (hardware) i Damir Prizmić (dizajn). NeoRetro Corner izložbena je selekcija neo i retro tehnologija iz Radionine kolekcije uređaja. BSides Zagreb 2026 je sigurnosna konferencija usmjerena na zajednicu, stvorena za istraživače, profesionalce i entuzijaste koji žele gostoljubivo mjesto za učenje i suradnju. Događaj okuplja ljude kako bi dijelili ideje, istraživali nove sigurnosne teme i povezivali se s drugima kojima je stalo do otvorenog znanja u kibernetičkoj sigurnosti. Budući da je konferencija u potpunosti volonterska i neprofitna, održava se opuštena i podržavajuća atmosfera u kojoj posjetitelji mogu sudjelovati u razgovorima, radionicama i raspravama koje vodi lokalna i regionalna sigurnosna zajednica. //////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// Radiona’s eBadge ZigZag and NeoRetro Corner program participates in the program of the international BSides Zagreb 2026 conference in Zagreb, which takes place on March 6, 2026. Radiona will be represented by Goran Mahovlić, Vlado Vince and others. ZigZag eBadge was developed by Goran Mahovlić (hardware) and Damir Prizmić (design). NeoRetro Corner is a showcase of neo and retro technologies from Radiona’s device collection. BSides Zagreb 2026 is a community-focused security conference, created for researchers, professionals, and enthusiasts who want a welcoming place to learn and collaborate. The event brings people together to share ideas, explore new security topics, and connect with others who care about open knowledge in cybersecurity. Since the conference is entirely volunteer-based and non-profit, it maintains a relaxed and supportive atmosphere where visitors can participate in talks, workshops, and discussions led by the local and regional security community.', '# eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corner @ BSides Zagreb 2026 Radionin program eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corner sudjeluje u programu međunarodne BSides Zagreb 2026 konferencije u Zagrebu koja se održava 6. ožujka 2026. Radionu će predstavljati Goran Mahovlić, Emard, Vlado Vince i dr. ZigZag eBadge razvili Goran Mahovlić (hardware) i Damir Prizmić (dizajn). NeoRetro Corner izložbena je selekcija neo i retro tehnologija iz Radionine kolekcije […] Radionin program eBadge ZigZag i NeoRetro Corne r sudjeluje u programu međunarodne BSides Zagreb 2026 konferencije u Zagrebu koja se održava 6. ožujka 2026. Radionu će predstavljati Goran Mahovlić, Emard, Vlado Vince i dr. ZigZag eBadge razvili Goran Mahovlić (hardware) i Damir Prizmić (dizajn). NeoRetro Corner izložbena je selekcija neo i retro tehnologija iz Radionine kolekcije uređaja. BSides Zagreb 2026 je sigurnosna konferencija usmjerena na zajednic');
